DG.put("ath-pakhyaan-charitr-likhyate/209",{"n":209,"title":null,"title_roman":null,"page":1833,"blocks":[{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1833,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[1],"number_text":"੧।","page":1833,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧਾਰਾ ਨਗਰੀ ਕੋ ਰਹੈ ਭਰਥਰਿ ਰਾਵ ਸੁਜਾਨ।","roman":"Dhaaraa nagree ko rahai bharathri raav sujaan |","meaning_en":"In the city of Dhara there lived the wise king Bharthari,","page":1833,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਧਾਰਾ ਨਗਰ ਵਿਚ ਭਰਥਰੀ ਨਾ ਦਾ ਇਕ ਸੁਜਾਨ ਰਾਜਾ ਰਹਿੰਦਾ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੋ ਦ੍ਵਾਦਸ ਬਿਦ੍ਯਾ ਨਿਪੁਨ ਸੂਰਬੀਰ ਬਲਵਾਨ। ੧।","roman":"Do dvaadas bidyaa nipun soorbeer balvaan | 1 |","meaning_en":"skilled in the fourteen sciences, a brave and mighty warrior.","page":1833,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦੋ ਦ੍ਵਾਦਸ: 'two and twelve', read as the fourteen branches of learning; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਚੌਦਾ ਵਿਦਿਆਵਾ ਵਿਚ ਨਿਪੁਣ ਅਤੇ ਸੂਰਵੀਰ ਤੇ ਬਲਵਾਨ ਸੀ ॥੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[2],"number_text":"੨।","page":1835,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਨ ਮਤੀ ਤਾ ਕੇ ਬਰ ਨਾਰੀ। ਪਿੰਗੁਲ ਦੇਇ ਪ੍ਰਾਨਨਿ ਤੇ ਪ੍ਯਾਰੀ।","roman":"Bhaan matee taa ke bar naaree | pingul dei praanni te pyaaree |","meaning_en":"Bhan Mati was his excellent wife, and Pingula was dearer to him than life.","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪਿੰਗੁਲ ਦੇਇ: printed 'Pingul Dei' here; the same queen as Pingula (also printed Pingulamati). Two queens are named, Bhan Mati and Pingula.","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਦੀ ਭਾਨ ਮਤੀ ਨਾ ਦੀ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਰਾਣੀ ਸੀ ਅਤੇ ਪਿੰਗੁਲ ਦੇਵੀ ਵੀ ਪ੍ਰਾਣਾ ਤੋਂ ਪਿਆਰੀ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਪ੍ਰਮਾਨ ਭਾ ਰਾਨੀ ਸੋਹੈ। ਦੇਵ ਅਦੇਵ ਸੁਤਾ ਢਿਗ ਕੋ ਹੈ। ੨।","roman":"Apramaan bhaa raanee sohai | dev adev sutaa dhig ko hai | 2 |","meaning_en":"The queen shone with measureless radiance; what were the daughters of gods and demons beside her?","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਣੀਆਂ ਦੀ ਅਨੂਪਮ ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ਸ਼ੋਭਦੀ ਸੀ। ਉਨ੍ਰਹਾ ਸਾਹਮਣੇ ਦੇਵਤਿਆਂ ਅਤੇ ਦੈਂਤਾ ਦੀਆਂ ਪੁੱਤਰੀਆਂ ਭਲਾ ਕੀ ਸਨ ॥੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[3],"number_text":"੩।","page":1835,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਨ ਮਤੀ ਕੀ ਅਧਿਕ ਛਬਿ ਜਲ ਥਲ ਰਹੀ ਸਮਾਇ।","roman":"Bhaan matee kee adhik chhabi jal thal rahee samaai |","meaning_en":"The great beauty of Bhan Mati filled water and land;","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਭਾਨ ਮਤੀ ਦੀ ਬਹੁਤ ਅਧਿਕ ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ਜਲ ਥਲ ਵਿਚ ਸਮਾ ਰਹੀ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਦੇਵ ਦਿਵਾਨੇ ਲਖਿ ਭਏ ਦਾਨਵ ਗਏ ਬਿਕਾਇ। ੩।","roman":"Dev divaane lakhi bhae daanav gae bikaai | 3 |","meaning_en":"the gods went mad at the sight of it, and the demons were sold into her service.","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਗਏ ਬਿਕਾਇ: 'were sold', i.e. became her slaves.","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਸ ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਦੇਵਤੇ ਦੀਵਾਨੇ ਹੋ ਗਏ ਸਨ ਅਤੇ ਦੈਂਤ ਤਾ (ਸਮਝੋ) ਵਿਕ ਹੀ ਗਏ ਸਨ ॥੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[4],"number_text":"੪।","page":1835,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਔਰ ਪਿੰਗੁਲਾਮਤੀ ਕੀ ਸੋਭਾ ਲਖੀ ਅਪਾਰ।","roman":"Aur pingulaamtee kee sobhaa lakhee apaar |","meaning_en":"And the loveliness of Pingula was seen to be boundless;","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪਿੰਗੁਲਾਮਤੀ: printed 'Pingulamati' here.","meaning_pa":"ਅਤੇ ਪਿੰਗੁਲ ਮਤੀ ਦੀ ਸ਼ੋਭਾ ਵੀ ਅਪਰ ਅਪਾਰ ਦਿਸਦੀ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗੜਿ ਚਤੁਰਾਨਨ ਤਵਨ ਸਮ ਔਰ ਨ ਸਕਿਯੋ ਸੁਧਾਰ। ੪।","roman":"Gari chaturaanan tavan sam aur na sakiyo sudhaar | 4 |","meaning_en":"having fashioned her, the four-faced one could not shape another like her.","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚਤੁਰਾਨਨ: Brahma.","meaning_pa":"(ਉਸ ਨੂੰ) ਬ੍ਰਹਮਾ ਨੇ ਬਣਾ ਕੇ ਫਿਰ ਉਸ ਵਰਗੀ ਹੋਰ ਕੋਈ ਨਾ ਬਣਾ ਸਕਿਆ ॥੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[5],"number_text":"੫।","page":1835,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕ ਦਿਵਸ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਗਯੋ ਸਿਕਾਰਾ। ਚਿਤ ਭੀਤਰ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਬਿਚਾਰਾ।","roman":"Ek divas nrip gayo sikaaraa | chit bheetar ih bhaati bichaaraa |","meaning_en":"One day the king went hunting, and thought in this way in his mind;","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਇਕ ਦਿਨ ਰਾਜਾ ਸ਼ਿਕਾਰ ਲਈ ਗਿਆ ਅਤੇ ਮਨ ਵਿਚ ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਵਿਚਾਰ ਕੀਤਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਸਤ੍ਰ ਬੋਰਿ ਸ੍ਰੋਨਤਹਿ ਪਠਾਏ। ਕਹਿਯੋ ਸਿੰਘ ਭਰਥਰ ਹਰਿ ਘਾਏ। ੫।","roman":"Basatr bori sronathi pathaae | kahiyo singh bharthar hari ghaae | 5 |","meaning_en":"he dipped his clothes in blood and sent them, saying, 'A lion has killed Bharthari.'","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਰਥਰ ਹਰਿ: the name Bhartrihari, printed in two words.","meaning_pa":"(ਉਸ ਨੇ ਆਪਣੇ) ਬਸਤ੍ਰ ਲਹੂ ਵਿਚ ਡਬੋ ਕੇ (ਘਰ) ਭੇਜ ਦਿੱਤੇ ਅਤੇ ਕਹਿਲਵਾ ਭੇਜਿਆ ਕਿ ਸ਼ੇਰ ਭਰਥਰ ਹਰਿ ਨੂੰ ਖਾ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ ॥੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[6],"number_text":"੬।","page":1835,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਸਤ੍ਰ ਭ੍ਰਿਤ ਲੈ ਸਦਨ ਸਿਧਾਰਿਯੋ। ਉਚਰਿਯੋ ਆਜੁ ਸਿੰਘ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਮਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Basatr bhrit lai sadan sidhaariyo | uchriyo aaju singh nrip maariyo |","meaning_en":"The servant took the clothes and went to the palace, and declared, 'Today a lion has killed the king.'","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਸਤ੍ਰ ਲੈ ਕੇ ਸੇਵਕ ਮਹੱਲ ਵਿਚ ਗਿਆ ਅਤੇ (ਜਾ ਕੇ) ਕਹਿਣ ਲਗਾ ਕਿ ਅਜ ਸ਼ੇਰ ਨੇ ਰਾਜੇ ਨੂੰ ਮਾਰ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਨੀ ਉਦਿਤ ਜਰਨ ਕੌ ਭਈ। ਹਾਇ ਉਚਰਿ ਪਿੰਗਲ ਮਰਿ ਗਈ। ੬।","roman":"Raanee udit jaran kau bhaee | haai uchri pingal mari gaee | 6 |","meaning_en":"The queen made ready to burn herself; Pingula cried 'Alas!' and died.","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"'The queen' is taken as Bhan Mati; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਣੀ (ਭਾਨ ਮਤੀ) ਸੜ ਮਰਨ ਲਈ ਤਤਪਰ ਹੋ ਗਈ ਅਤੇ ਪਿੰਗੁਲਮਤੀ (ਕੇਵਲ) ਹਾਇ ਕਹਿ ਕੇ ਮਰ ਗਈ ॥੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[7],"number_text":"੭।","page":1835,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਰਿਯਾ ਨ ਤਵਨ ਸਰਾਹੀਯਹਿ ਕਰਤ ਅਗਨਿ ਮੈ ਪਯਾਨ।","roman":"Triyaa na tavan saraaheeyhi karat agni mai payaan |","meaning_en":"That woman is not the one to be praised who makes her way into the fire;","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਇਸਤਰੀ ਦੀ ਸ਼ਲਾਘਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਕਰਨੀ ਚਾਹੀਦੀ ਜੋ ਅਗਨੀ ਵਿਚ ਪ੍ਰਵੇਸ਼ ਕਰਦੀ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧੰਨ੍ਯ ਧੰਨ੍ਯ ਅਬਲਾ ਤੇਈ ਬਧਤ ਬਿਰਹ ਕੇ ਬਾਨ। ੭।","roman":"Dhanny dhanny ablaa te'ee badhat birah ke baan | 7 |","meaning_en":"blessed, blessed are those women who are slain by the arrows of separation.","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਧੰਨ ਧੰਨ ਤਾ ਉਹ ਇਸਤਰੀ ਹੈ ਜੋ ਬਿਰਹੋਂ ਦੇ ਬਾਣ ਨਾਲ ਹੀ ਵਿੰਨ੍ਰਹੀ ਜਾਦੀ ਹੈ ॥੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਅੜਿਲ","gurmukhi":"ਅੜਿਲ","roman":"Aril","meaning_en":"Arril.","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੜਿਲ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[8],"number_text":"੮।","page":1835,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਖੇਲਿ ਅਖੇਟਕ ਜਬ ਭਰਥਰਿ ਘਰਿ ਆਇਯੋ।","roman":"Kheli akhetak jab bharathri ghari aaiyo |","meaning_en":"When Bharthari came home after the hunt,","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸ਼ਿਕਾਰ ਖੇਡ ਕੇ ਜਦ ਭਰਥਰੀ ਘਰ ਪਰਤਿਆ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਾਇ ਕਰਤ ਪਿੰਗੁਲਾ ਮਰੀ ਸੁਨਿ ਪਾਇਯੋ।","roman":"Haai karat pingulaa maree suni paaiyo |","meaning_en":"he heard that Pingula had died crying 'Alas!'","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਤਾ ਉਸ ਨੇ) ਸੁਣਿਆ ਕਿ ਪਿੰਗੁਲਾਮਤੀ 'ਹਾਇ' ਕਹਿੰਦੀ ਹੋਈ ਮਰ ਗਈ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਡਾਰਿ ਡਾਰਿ ਸਿਰ ਧੂਰਿ ਹਾਇ ਰਾਜਾ ਕਹੈ।","roman":"Daari daari sir dhoori haai raajaa kahai |","meaning_en":"Throwing dust again and again on his head, the king cried 'Alas!","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਿਰ ਵਿਚ ਖੇਹ ਪਾ ਪਾ ਕੇ ਰਾਜਾ ਹਾਇ ਹਾਇ ਕਹਿਣ ਲਗਾ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਪਠੈ ਬਸਤ੍ਰ ਜਿਹ ਸਮੈ ਸਮੋ ਸੌ ਨ ਲਹੈ। ੮।","roman":"Ho pathai basatr jih samai samo sau na lahai | 8 |","meaning_en":"The moment in which I sent the clothes - that moment I cannot get back.'","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਮੋ ਸੌ ਨ ਲਹੈ: 'that time is not found'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਕਿ ਉਹ ਸਮਾ ਹੁਣ ਹੱਥ ਨਹੀਂ ਆਉਾਂਦਾ ਜਿਸ ਸਮੇਾਂ ਮੈਂ ਬਸਤ੍ਰ ਘਰ ਭੇਜੇ ਸਨ ॥੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[9],"number_text":"੯।","page":1835,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੈ ਮੈ ਆਜੁ ਕਟਾਰੀ ਮਾਰੌ। ਹ੍ਵੈ ਜੋਗੀ ਸਭ ਹੀ ਘਰ ਜਾਰੌ।","roman":"Kai mai aaju kataaree maarau | hvai jogee sabh hee ghar jaarau |","meaning_en":"'Either I will strike myself with a dagger today, or become a yogi and burn the whole house.","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਾ ਤਾ ਮੈਂ ਕਟਾਰੀ ਮਾਰ ਕੇ ਮਰ ਜਾਵਾਗਾ, ਜਾ ਜੋਗੀ ਬਣ ਕੇ ਸਾਰਾ ਘਰ ਸਾੜ ਦਿਆਂਗਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧ੍ਰਿਗ ਮੇਰੋ ਜਿਯਬੋ ਜਗ ਮਾਹੀ। ਜਾ ਕੇ ਨਾਰਿ ਪਿੰਗੁਲਾ ਨਾਹੀ। ੯।","roman":"Dhrig mero jiybo jag maahee | jaa ke naari pingulaa naahee | 9 |","meaning_en":"Cursed is my living in the world, who have not my wife Pingula.'","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਗਤ ਵਿਚ ਮੇਰੇ ਜੀਣੇ ਨੂੰ ਧਿੱਕਾਰ ਹੈ ਜਿਸ ਦੇ (ਘਰ) ਪਿੰਗੁਲਾ ਰਾਣੀ ਨਹੀਂ ਹੈ ॥੯॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[10],"number_text":"੧੦।","page":1835,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਭੂਖਨ ਬਹੁ ਮੋਲ ਕੇ ਅੰਗਨ ਅਧਿਕ ਸੁਹਾਹਿ।","roman":"Jo bhookhan bahu mol ke angan adhik suhaahi |","meaning_en":"The ornaments of great price that looked so fine upon the limbs","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜੋ ਵਡ-ਮੁਲੇ ਗਹਿਣੇ ਅੰਗਾ ਨੂੰ ਬਹੁਤ ਸੁਸਜਿਤ ਕਰਦੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੇ ਅਬ ਨਾਗਨਿ ਸੇ ਭਏ ਕਾਟਿ ਕਾਟਿ ਤਨ ਖਾਹਿ। ੧੦।","roman":"Te ab naagni se bhae kaati kaati tan khaahi | 10 |","meaning_en":"have now become like she-snakes; they bite and eat the body.","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਹੁਣ ਨਾਗਾ ਵਰਗੇ ਹੋ ਗਏ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਸ਼ਰੀਰ ਨੂੰ ਕਟ ਕਟ ਕੇ ਖਾਦੇ ਹਨ ॥੧੦॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਵੈਯਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[11],"number_text":"੧੧।","page":1835,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਂਕ ਸੀ ਬੀਨ ਸਿੰਗਾਰ ਅੰਗਾਰ ਸੇ ਤਾਲ ਮ੍ਰਿਦੰਗ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਕਟਾਰੇ।","roman":"Baank see been singaar angaar se taal mridang kripaan kataare |","meaning_en":"The veena is like a curved dagger, adornments are like burning coals, the cymbals and drum are swords and daggers;","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਾਂਕ: a curved dagger. Verses 11-13 list pleasant things that have turned painful; many comparisons are compressed and uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਬੀਨ 'ਬਾਕ' (ਤਲਵਾਰ) ਵਰਗੀ, ਸ਼ਿੰਗਾਰ ਅੰਗਾਰਿਆਂ ਜਿਹੇ ਅਤੇ ਤਾਲ ਤੇ ਮ੍ਰਿਦੰਗ ਕ੍ਰਿਪਾਨ ਅਤੇ ਕਟਾਰ ਦੇ ਸਮਾਨ ਲਗਦੇ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜ੍ਵਾਲ ਸੀ ਜੌਨਿ ਜੁਡਾਈ ਸੀ ਜੇਬ ਸਖੀ ਘਨਸਾਰ ਕਿਸਾਰ ਕੇ ਆਰੇ।","roman":"Jvaal see jauni judaaee see jeb sakhee ghansaar kisaar ke aare |","meaning_en":"the moonlight is like flame, beauty like a shivering fever, O friend, and camphor like the teeth of a saw;","page":1835,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜੁਡਾਈ: read as 'ague, cold fever'; ਜੇਬ: 'beauty, grace'; ਕਿਸਾਰ ਕੇ ਆਰੇ: read as 'saws'; all uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਹੇ ਸਖੀ! ਚਾਦਨੀ ਅੱਗ ਵਰਗੀ, ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ('ਜੇਬ') ਕੁਹਰੇ ('ਜੁਡਾਈ') ਜਿਹੀ ਅਤੇ ਮੁਸ਼ਕ ਕਪੂਰ ਆਰੇ ਦੇ ਤਿਖੇ ਦੰਦਿਆਂ (ਨੋਕਾ) ਦੇ ਸਮਾਨ ਹਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੋਗ ਸੋ ਰਾਗ ਬਿਰਾਗ ਸੋ ਬੋਲ ਬਬਾਰਿਦ ਬੂੰਦਨ ਬਾਨ ਬਿਸਾਰੇ।","roman":"Rog so raag biraag so bol babaarid boondan baan bisaare |","meaning_en":"music is like sickness, speech like grief, and the drops from the clouds are poisoned arrows;","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਿਰਾਗ: here 'sorrow'; ਬਬਾਰਿਦ: read as ਬਾਰਿਦ 'cloud'; ਬਿਸਾਰੇ: 'poisoned'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਗ ਰੋਗ ਵਰਗਾ, ਬੋਲ ਬੈਰਾਗ ਜਿਹੇ, ਬਦਲ ਦੀਆਂ ਕਣੀਆਂ ਵਿਸ਼-ਬੁਝੇ ਤੀਰਾ ਦੇ ਸਮਾਨ ਹਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਨ ਸੇ ਬੈਨ ਭਾਲਾ ਜੈਸੇ ਭੂਖਨ ਹਾਰਨ ਹੋਹਿ ਭੁਜੰਗਨ ਕਾਰੇ। ੧੧।","roman":"Baan se bain bhaalaa jaise bhookhan haaran hohi bhujangan kaare | 11 |","meaning_en":"words are like arrows, ornaments like spears, and necklaces become black serpents.","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬੋਲ ਤੀਰਾ ਵਰਗੇ, ਗਹਿਣੇ ਭਾਲਿਆਂ ਜਿਹੇ ਅਤੇ ਹਾਰ ਕਾਲੇ ਸੱਪਾ ਦੇ ਸਮਾਨ ਹੋ ਗਏ ਹਨ ॥੧੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[12],"number_text":"੧੨।","page":1837,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਂਕ ਸੇ ਬੈਨ ਬ੍ਰਿਲਾਪ ਸੇ ਬਾਰਨ ਬ੍ਯਾਧ ਸੀ ਬਾਸ ਬਿਯਾਰ ਬਹੀ ਰੀ।","roman":"Baank se bain brilaap se baaran byaadh see baas biyaar bahee ree |","meaning_en":"Words are like daggers, songs like lamentation, and the fragrant breeze blows like a disease, O friend;","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਾਰਨ: unclear; read loosely as 'songs/sounds'; ਬ੍ਯਾਧ: 'disease' (or 'hunter'); uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਬੋਲ ਤਲਵਾਰ ਵਰਗੇ, ਵਾਜਿਆਂ ਦੀ ਧੁਨ ('ਬਾਰਨ') ਵਿਰਲਾਪ ਦੇ ਸਮਾਨ ਅਤੇ ਵਗਦੀ ਹੋਈ ਹਵਾ ਦੀ ਬਾਸ ਵੱਡੇ ਰੋਗ ਜਿਹੀ ਲਗਦੀ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਕ ਸੀ ਕੋਕਿਲ ਕੂਕ ਕਰਾਲ ਮ੍ਰਿਨਾਲ ਕਿ ਬ੍ਯਾਲ ਘਰੀ ਕਿ ਛੁਰੀ ਰੀ।","roman":"Kaak see kokil kook karaal mrinaal ki byaal gharee ki chhuree ree |","meaning_en":"the cuckoo's call is dreadful, like a crow's; is it a lotus-stalk or a snake, an hour or a knife, O friend?","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਘਰੀ: 'hour' (a ghari); uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਕੋਇਲ ਦੀ ਕੂਕ ਕਰਕਸ਼ ਕਾ ਕਾ ਵਰਗੀ, ਕਮਲ ਦੀ ਡੰਡੀ ਸੱਪ ਜਿਹੀ ਅਤੇ ਇਕ ਘੜੀ ਛੁਰੀ ਦੇ ਸਮਾਨ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਰ ਸੀ ਭੌਨ ਭਯਾਨਕ ਭੂਖਨ ਜੌਨ ਕੀ ਜ੍ਵਾਲ ਸੌ ਜਾਤ ਜਰੀ ਰੀ।","roman":"Bhaar see bhaun bhayaanak bhookhan jaun kee jvaal sau jaat jaree ree |","meaning_en":"The house is like a furnace, the ornaments are fearful, and one is burned by the flame of the moonlight, O friend;","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਾਰ: read as ਭਾੜ, a parching-oven; ਜੌਨ: moonlight.","meaning_pa":"ਭੌਆਂ ('ਭੌਨ') ਭਠੀ ਵਰਗੀਆਂ (ਲਗਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ) ਗਹਿਣੇ ਭਿਆਨਕ (ਪ੍ਰਤੀਤ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ) ਅਤੇ ਚੰਨ ਦੀ ਚਾਨਣੀ ਨਾਲ ਸੜਦੀ ਜਾ ਰਹੀ ਹਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਨ ਸੀ ਬੀਨ ਬਿਨਾ ਉਹਿ ਬਾਲ ਬਸੰਤ ਕੋ ਅੰਤਕਿ ਅੰਤ ਸਖੀ ਰੀ। ੧੨।","roman":"Baan see been binaa uhi baal basant ko antki ant sakhee ree | 12 |","meaning_en":"the veena is like an arrow; without that lady, O friend, spring is the very end of ends.","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅੰਤਕਿ ਅੰਤ: 'the death of death' or 'death itself'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਹੇ ਸਖੀ! ਬੀਨ ਤੀਰ ਵਰਗੀ ਲਗਦੀ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਉਸ ਇਸਤਰੀ ਤੋਂ ਬਿਨਾ ਬਸੰਤ ਤਾ ਮਾਨੋ ਅੰਤ ਹੀ ਹੋ ਗਿਆ ਹੋਵੇ ॥੧੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[13],"number_text":"੧੩।","page":1837,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬੈਰੀ ਸੀ ਬ੍ਯਾਰ ਬ੍ਰਿਲਾਪ ਸੌ ਬੋਲ ਬਬਾਨ ਸੀ ਬੀਨ ਬਜੰਤ ਬਿਥਾਰੇ।","roman":"Bairee see byaar brilaap sau bol babaan see been bajant bithaare |","meaning_en":"The breeze is like an enemy, speech like lamentation, and the sounding veena spreads pain like an arrow;","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਬਾਨ: read as ਬਾਨ 'arrow'; ਬਿਥਾਰੇ: 'spreads' or 'painful'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਪੌਣ ਵੈਰੀ ਵਰਗੀ, ਬੋਲ ਵਿਰਲਾਪ ਵਰਗੇ, ਬੀਨ ਬਾਣ ਦੇ ਸਮਾਨ ਵਿਅਰਥ ਵਿਚ ਵਜਦੀ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੰਗ ਸੇ ਜੰਗ ਮੁਚੰਗ ਦੁਖੰਗ ਅਨੰਗ ਕਿ ਅੰਕਸੁ ਆਕ ਕਿਆਰੇ।","roman":"Jang se jang muchang dukhang anang ki anksu aak kiaare |","meaning_en":"the bells are like war, the muchang hurts the limbs, and the flower-beds are the love-god's goad or beds of bitter aak;","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜੰਗ ਸੇ ਜੰਗ: 'jang (bells) like jang (war)'; ਦੁਖੰਗ: 'paining the body'; ਆਕ: the bitter milkweed; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਸੰਖ ਯੁੱਧ ਵਰਗੇ, ਮੁਚੰਗ ਸ਼ਰੀਰ ਨੂੰ ਦੁਖ ਦੇਣ ਵਾਲਾ ('ਦੁਖੰਗ') ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਕਾਮ ਦੇਵ ਦਾ ਦਬਾਓ ਅੱਕ ਵਰਗਾ ਦੁਖਦਾਈ ਜਾ ਕੌੜਾ ('ਕਿਆਰੇ') ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਾਂਦਨੀ ਚੰਦ ਚਿਤਾ ਚਹੂੰ ਓਰ ਸੁ ਕੋਕਿਲਾ ਕੂਕ ਕਿ ਹੂਕ ਸੀ ਮਾਰੇ।","roman":"Chaandnee chand chitaa chahoon or su kokilaa kook ki hook see maare |","meaning_en":"the light of the moon is a funeral pyre on all four sides, and the call of the cuckoo strikes like a stab of pain;","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹੂਕ: a pang.","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਹਾ ਪਾਸਿਆਂ ਵਿਚ ਪਸਰੀ ਹੋਈ ਚਾਦਨੀ ਚਿਤਾ ਵਰਗੀ ਲਗਦੀ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਕੋਇਲ ਦਾ ਕੂਕ ਮਾਰਨਾ ਪੀੜ ਦੀ ਕਸਕ ਦੇ ਸਮਾਨ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਰ ਸੇ ਭੌਨ ਭਯਾਨਕ ਭੂਖਨ ਫੂਲੇ ਨ ਫੂਲ ਫਨੀ ਫਨਿਯਾਰੇ। ੧੩।","roman":"Bhaar se bhaun bhayaanak bhookhan phoole na phool phanee phaniyaare | 13 |","meaning_en":"the house is like a furnace, the ornaments are fearful; these are not flowers in bloom but hooded serpents.","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਭਵਨ ਭਠੀ ਵਰਗੇ, ਗਹਿਣੇ ਭਿਆਨਕ ਹਨ ਖਿੜੇ ਹੋਏ ਫੁਲ ਫੁਲ ਨਹੀਂ, ਸਗੋਂ ਸੱਪਾ ਦੇ ਫਨ ਦੇ ਸਮਾਨ ਹਨ ॥੧੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[14],"number_text":"੧੪।","page":1837,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਹਠਿ ਹਾਥ ਸਿੰਧੌਰਾ ਧਰਿ ਹੌ। ਪਿੰਗੁਲ ਹੇਤ ਅਗਨਿ ਮਹਿ ਜਰਿ ਹੌ।","roman":"Ho hathi haath sindhauraa dhari hau | pingul het agni mahi jari hau |","meaning_en":"'I will resolutely take the sindhaura in my hand, and burn in the fire for the sake of Pingula.","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਿੰਧੌਰਾ: the vermilion-box (or coconut) held by one about to burn on a pyre. ਹੋ: here read as 'I' (ਹੌ) or the vocative; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਮੈਂ ਹਠ ਪੂਰਵਕ ਹੱਥ ਵਿਚ ਸਿੰਧੌਰਾ ਧਾਰਨ ਕਰ ਕੇ ਪਿੰਗੁਲਮਤੀ ਲਈ ਅਗਨੀ ਵਿਚ ਸੜਾਗਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੌ ਇਹ ਆਜੁ ਚੰਚਲਾ ਜੀਯੈ। ਤਬ ਭਰਥਰੀ ਪਾਨਿ ਕੌ ਪੀਯੈ। ੧੪।","roman":"Jau ih aaju chanchlaa jeeyai | tab bharathree paani kau peeyai | 14 |","meaning_en":"Only if this lady were to live today would Bharthari drink water.'","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜੇ ਇਹ ਇਸਤਰੀ ਅਜ ਜੀ ਪਏ, ਤਦ ਭਰਥਰੀ ਪਾਣੀ ਗ੍ਰਹਿਣ ਕਰੇਗਾ ॥੧੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਅੜਿਲ","gurmukhi":"ਅੜਿਲ","roman":"Aril","meaning_en":"Arril.","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੜਿਲ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[15],"number_text":"੧੫।","page":1837,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤਬ ਤਹ ਗੋਰਖਨਾਥ ਪਹੂੰਚ੍ਯੋ ਆਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Tab tah gorakhnaath pahoonchyo aai kai |","meaning_en":"Then Gorakhnath arrived at that place;","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਦ ਉਥੇ ਗੋਰਖਨਾਥ ਆ ਪਹੁੰਚਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਪ੍ਰਤਿ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਅਦੇਸੁ ਸੁ ਨਾਦ ਬਜਾਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Nrip prati kahiyo adesu su naad bajaai kai |","meaning_en":"sounding his horn, he said 'Ades' to the king.","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਦੇਸੁ: 'Ades', the yogis' greeting.","meaning_pa":"(ਉਸ ਨੇ) ਸਿੰਗੀ ਵਜਾ ਕੇ ਰਾਜੇ ਪ੍ਰਤਿ 'ਆਦੇਸ' ਦਿੱਤਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਨੀ ਦਈ ਜਿਵਾਇ ਸਰੂਪ ਅਨੇਕ ਧਰਿ।","roman":"Raanee daee jivaai saroop anek dhari |","meaning_en":"He brought the queen back to life, making many forms of her:","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਗੋਰਖਨਾਥ ਨੇ) ਰਾਣੀ ਨੂੰ ਅਨੇਕ ਸਰੂਪ ਧਾਰਨ ਕਰ ਕੇ ਜੀਵਿਤ ਕਰ ਦਿੱਤਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਸੁਨਹੋ ਭਰਥਰਿ ਰਾਵ ਲੇਹੁ ਗਹਿ ਏਕ ਕਰੁ। ੧੫।","roman":"Ho sunho bharathri raav lehu gahi ek karu | 15 |","meaning_en":"'Listen, King Bharthari: take hold of one of them by the hand.'","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹੇ ਭਰਥਰੀ ਰਾਜੇ! ਸੁਣੋ, (ਇਨ੍ਰਹਾ ਵਿਚੋਂ) ਹੱਥ ਨਾਲ ਇਕ ਪਕੜ ਲਵੋ ॥੧੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਭਰਥਰਿ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਭਰਥਰਿ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Bharathri baach","meaning_en":"Bharthari said:","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਭਰਥਰੀ ਨੇ ਕਿਹਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[16],"number_text":"੧੬।","page":1837,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਹ ਗਹੌ ਕੌਨੇ ਤਜੌ ਚਿਤ ਮੈ ਕਰੈ ਬਿਬੇਕ।","roman":"Kaah gahau kaune tajau chit mai karai bibek |","meaning_en":"'Which should I take and which leave? I weigh it in my mind;","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਸ ਨੂੰ ਪਕੜਾ ਅਤੇ ਕਿਹੜੀ ਨੂੰ ਛਡਾ, (ਮੈਂ) ਚਿਤ ਵਿਚ ਸੋਚ ਕਰ ਰਿਹਾ ਹਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਭੈ ਪਿੰਗੁਲਾ ਕੀ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਰਾਨੀ ਭਈ ਅਨੇਕ। ੧੬।","roman":"Sabhai pingulaa kee prabhaa raanee bhaee anek | 16 |","meaning_en":"all have the radiance of Pingula; the queen has become many.'","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰੀਆਂ ਹੀ ਪਿੰਗੁਲਾ ਦੀ ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ਵਰਗੀਆਂ ਅਨੇਕ ਰਾਣੀਆਂ ਬਣ ਗਈਆਂ ਹਨ ॥੧੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਅੜਿਲ","gurmukhi":"ਅੜਿਲ","roman":"Aril","meaning_en":"Arril.","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੜਿਲ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[17],"number_text":"੧੭।","page":1837,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯੌ ਕਹਿ ਗੋਰਖ ਨਾਥ ਤਹਾ ਤੇ ਜਾਤ ਭਯੋ।","roman":"Yau kahi gorakh naath tahaa te jaat bhayo |","meaning_en":"Having said this, Gorakhnath went away from there.","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"'Having said this' is printed after Bharthari's words; translated as printed.","meaning_pa":"ਇਹ ਕਹਿ ਕੇ ਗੋਰਖ ਨਾਥ ਉਥੋਂ ਚਲਿਆ ਗਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਨ ਮਤੀ ਕੋ ਚਿਤ ਚੰਡਾਰ ਇਕ ਹਰ ਲਿਯੋ।","roman":"Bhaan matee ko chit chandaar ik har liyo |","meaning_en":"A chandal stole away the heart of Bhan Mati.","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚੰਡਾਰ: a chandal, a man of the lowest caste.","meaning_pa":"(ਇਧਰ) ਭਾਨ ਮਤੀ ਦਾ ਚਿਤ ਇਕ ਚੰਡਾਲ ਨੇ ਹਰ ਲਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਦਿਨ ਤੇ ਰਾਜਾ ਕੌ ਦਿਯੋ ਭੁਲਾਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Taa din te raajaa kau diyo bhulaai kai |","meaning_en":"From that day she put the king out of her mind;","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਦਿਨ ਤੋਂ (ਰਾਣੀ ਨੇ) ਰਾਜੇ ਨੂੰ ਭੁਲਾ ਦਿੱਤਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਰਾਨੀ ਨੀਚ ਕੇ ਰੂਪ ਰਹੀ ਉਰਝਾਇ ਕੈ। ੧੭।","roman":"Ho raanee neech ke roop rahee urjhaai kai | 17 |","meaning_en":"the queen remained entangled in the looks of the low-born man.","page":1837,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਣੀ (ਉਸ) ਨੀਚ ਦੇ ਰੂਪ ਵਿਚ ਉਲਝ ਕੇ ਰਹਿ ਗਈ ॥੧੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[18],"number_text":"੧੮।","page":1839,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੂਤਮਤੀ ਦਾਸੀ ਹੁਤੀ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਲਈ ਬੁਲਾਇ।","roman":"Dootamtee daasee hutee tab hee laee bulaai |","meaning_en":"There was a maid named Dut Mati; she called her at once,","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਉਸ ਦੀ) ਦੂਤਮਤੀ ਨਾ ਦੀ ਇਕ ਦਾਸੀ ਸੀ। (ਉਸ ਨੂੰ) ਉਸੇ ਵੇਲੇ ਬੁਲਾ ਲਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਠੈ ਦੇਤ ਭੀ ਨੀਚ ਸੌ ਪਰਮ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਉਪਜਾਇ। ੧੮।","roman":"Pathai det bhee neech sau param preeti upjaai | 18 |","meaning_en":"and sent her to the low-born man, great love having risen in her.","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਨੀਚ ਨਾਲ ਬਹੁਤ ਪ੍ਰੀਤ ਪੈਦਾ ਕਰ ਕੇ (ਬੁਲਾਉਣ ਲਈ) ਭੇਜ ਦਿੱਤਾ ॥੧੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[19],"number_text":"੧੯।","page":1839,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਬ ਦੂਤੀ ਤਹ ਤੇ ਫਿਰਿ ਆਈ। ਯੌ ਪੂਛੌ ਰਾਨੀ ਤਿਹ ਜਾਈ।","roman":"Jab dootee tah te phiri aaee | yau poochhau raanee tih jaaee |","meaning_en":"When the go-between came back from there, the queen went and asked her this:","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਦ ਦੂਤੀ ਉਥੋਂ ਪਰਤ ਕੇ ਆਈ, ਤਾ ਰਾਣੀ ਨੇ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਜਾ ਕੇ ਪੁਛਿਆ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੁ ਅਲਿ ਮੀਤ ਕਬੈ ਹ੍ਯਾ ਐ ਹੈ। ਹਮਰੇ ਚਿਤ ਕੋ ਤਾਪ ਮਿਟੈ ਹੈ। ੧੯।","roman":"Kahu ali meet kabai hyaa ai hai | hamre chit ko taap mitai hai | 19 |","meaning_en":"'Tell me, friend, when will my friend come here and take away the burning of my heart?","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹੇ ਸਖੀ! ਦਸ, (ਮੇਰਾ) ਮਿਤਰ ਇਥੇ ਕਦ ਆਵੇਗਾ ਅਤੇ ਮੇਰੇ ਚਿਤ ਦਾ ਤਾਪ ਮਿਟਾਏਗਾ ॥੧੯॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਅੜਿਲ","gurmukhi":"ਅੜਿਲ","roman":"Aril","meaning_en":"Arril.","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੜਿਲ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[20],"number_text":"੨੦।","page":1839,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੁ ਨ ਸਹਚਰੀ ਸਾਚੁ ਸਜਨੁ ਕਬ ਆਇ ਹੈ।","roman":"Kahu na sahachree saachu sajnu kab aai hai |","meaning_en":"Tell me truly, companion, when will my dear one come?","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹੇ ਸਖੀ! ਸਚ ਦਸ ਨ, ਸੱਜਨ ਕਦ ਆਵੇਗਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋਰ ਨੈਨ ਸੌ ਨੈਨ ਕਬੈ ਮੁਸਕਾਇ ਹੈ।","roman":"Jor nain sau nain kabai muskaai hai |","meaning_en":"When will he join his eyes with my eyes and smile?","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਮੇਰੇ) ਨੈਣਾ ਨਾਲ ਨੈਣ ਮਿਲਾ ਕੇ ਕਦ ਮੁਸਕਰਾਏਗਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਪਟਿ ਲਪਟਿ ਕਰਿ ਜਾਉ ਲਲਾ ਸੌ ਤੌਨ ਛਿਨ।","roman":"Lapti lapti kari jaau lalaa sau taun chhin |","meaning_en":"In that moment I shall cling and cling to my darling.","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਵੇਲੇ ਮੈਂ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਮ ਨਾਲ ਲਿਪਟ ਲਿਪਟ (ਕੇ ਆਨੰਦਿਤ ਹੋ) ਜਾਵਾਗੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਕਹੋ ਸਖੀ ਮੁਹਿ ਮੀਤ ਕਬੈ ਹੈ ਕਵਨ ਦਿਨ। ੨੦।","roman":"Ho kaho sakhee muhi meet kabai hai kavan din | 20 |","meaning_en":"Tell me, friend: when, on what day, will my friend be here?","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹੇ ਸਖੀ! ਦਸ, ਮੇਰਾ ਮਿਤਰ ਕਦੋਂ ਅਤੇ ਕਿਹੜੇ ਦਿਨ ਆਵੇਗਾ ॥੨੦॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[21],"number_text":"੨੧।","page":1839,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਰ ਬਾਰ ਗਜ ਮੁਤਿਯਨ ਗੁਹੌ ਬਨਾਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Baar baar gaj mutiyan guhau banaai kai |","meaning_en":"I would string elephant-pearls in every single hair,","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਾਰ ਬਾਰ: 'hair by hair' (or 'again and again'). ਗਜ ਮੁਤਿਯਨ: pearls said to come from an elephant's temple.","meaning_pa":"(ਮੈਂ) ਆਪਣੇ ਵਾਲ ਵਾਲ ਵਿਚ ਗਜ-ਮੋਤੀਆਂ (ਹਾਥੀ ਦੇ ਸਿਰ ਵਿਚੋਂ ਨਿਕਲੇ ਕਲਪਿਤ ਮੋਤੀਆਂ) ਨੂੰ ਚੰਗੀ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਗੁੰਦਾਗੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਪਨੇ ਲਲਾ ਕੋ ਛਿਨ ਮੈ ਲੇਉ ਰਿਝਾਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Apne lalaa ko chhin mai leu rijhaai kai |","meaning_en":"and in a moment win the delight of my darling.","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਮੈਂ) ਆਪਣੇ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਮ ਨੂੰ ਛਿਣ ਭਰ ਵਿਚ ਰਿਝਾ ਲਵਾਗੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਟੂਕ ਟੂਕ ਤਨ ਹੋਇ ਨ ਮੇਰੋ ਨੈਕ ਮਨ।","roman":"Took took tan hoi na mero naik man |","meaning_en":"Though my body were cut to pieces, my mind would not turn in the least;","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਨ ਮੇਰੋ: printed so; read as 'would not turn' (ਨ ਮੋਰੋ); uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਜੇ ਮੇਰਾ ਸ਼ਰੀਰ ਟੋਟੇ ਟੋਟੇ ਹੋ ਜਾਵੇ ਤਾ ਵੀ (ਮੈਂ ਆਪਣਾ) ਮਨ ਨਹੀਂ ਮੋੜਾਗੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਕਾਸੀ ਕਰਵਤ ਲਿਯੋ ਪ੍ਰਿਯਾ ਕੀ ਪ੍ਰੀਤ ਤਨ। ੨੧।","roman":"Ho kaasee karvat liyo priyaa kee preet tan | 21 |","meaning_en":"for love of my dear one I would take the saw at Kashi upon my body.","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਾਸੀ ਕਰਵਤ: the saw at Kashi, under which devotees were said to be cut in two. ਪ੍ਰਿਯਾ: printed in the feminine; the lover is meant.","meaning_pa":"ਪ੍ਰਿਯ ਦੀ ਪ੍ਰੀਤ ਲਈ ਕਾਸ਼ੀ ਦਾ ਕਲਵਤ੍ਰ ਵੀ ਤਨ ਉਤੇ ਸਹਿ ਲਵਾਗੀ ॥੨੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[22],"number_text":"੨੨।","page":1839,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਹਸਿ ਬਿਹਸਿ ਕਬ ਗਰੇ ਹਮਾਰੇ ਲਾਗਿ ਹੈ।","roman":"Bihsi bihsi kab gare hamaare laagi hai |","meaning_en":"When will he laugh and laugh and hold me round the neck?","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹੇ ਸਖੀ! ਉਹ ਕਦੋਂ ਹਸ ਹਸ ਕੇ ਮੇਰੇ ਗਲ ਨਾਲ ਲਗੇਗਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਬ ਹੀ ਸਭ ਹੀ ਸੋਕ ਹਮਾਰੇ ਭਾਗਿ ਹੈ।","roman":"Tab hee sabh hee sok hamaare bhaagi hai |","meaning_en":"Then at once all my sorrows will flee.","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਦੋਂ ਹੀ ਮੇਰੇ ਸਾਰੇ ਦੁਖ ਦੂਰ ਹੋ ਜਾਣਗੇ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਟਕ ਚਟਕ ਦੈ ਬਾਤੈ ਮਟਕਿ ਬਤਾਇ ਹੈ।","roman":"Chatak chatak dai baatai matki bataai hai |","meaning_en":"When he snaps his fingers and talks with playful gestures,","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚਟਕ ਚਟਕ ਦੈ: 'giving snap after snap'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"(ਮੇਰੇ ਨਾਲ ਜਦ ਉਹ) ਚਟਕ ਚਟਕ ਕੇ ਅਤੇ ਮਟਕ ਮਟਕ ਕੇ ਗੱਲਾ ਕਰੇਗਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਤਾ ਦਿਨ ਸਖੀ ਸਹਿਤ ਹਮ ਬਲਿ ਬਲਿ ਜਾਇ ਹੈ। ੨੨।","roman":"Ho taa din sakhee sahit ham bali bali jaai hai | 22 |","meaning_en":"on that day, friend, I and you with me will be a sacrifice to him.","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਖੀ ਸਹਿਤ: 'together with my friend'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਦਿਨ ਮੈਂ ਉਸ ਉਤੋਂ ਬਲਿਹਾਰ ਬਲਿਹਾਰ ਜਾਵਾਗੀ ॥੨੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[23],"number_text":"੨੩।","page":1839,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੌ ਐਸੇ ਝਰਿ ਮਿਲੈ ਸਜਨ ਸਖਿ ਆਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Jau aise jhari milai sajan sakhi aai kai |","meaning_en":"If my dear one comes and meets me so, O friend, in a rush,","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਝਰਿ: read as 'in a shower, all at once'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਹੇ ਸਖੀ! (ਜਦੋਂ ਮੈਨੂੰ) ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਆ ਕੇ ਸਜਨ ਮਿਲਣ ਲਈ ਟਪਕ ਪਵੇਗਾ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੋ ਮਨ ਕੌ ਲੈ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਜਾਇ ਚੁਰਾਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Mo man kau lai tab hee jaai churaai kai |","meaning_en":"he will steal my heart away that very moment.","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਾ ਮੇਰੇ ਮਨ ਨੂੰ ਤੁਰਤ ਚੁਰਾ ਕੇ ਲੈ ਜਾਏਗਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਤਿ ਭਾਤਿ ਰਤਿ ਕਰੌ ਨ ਛੋਰੋ ਏਕ ਛਿਨ।","roman":"Bhaati bhaati rati karau na chhoro ek chhin |","meaning_en":"I shall make love in many ways and not let him go for a single instant;","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਮੈਂ) ਉਸ ਨਾਲ ਭਾਤ ਭਾਤ ਦੀ ਰਤੀ-ਕ੍ਰੀੜਾ ਕਰਾਗੀ ਅਤੇ ਇਕ ਛਿਣ ਲਈ ਵੀ ਨਹੀਂ ਛਡਾਗੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਬੀਤੈ ਮਾਸ ਪਚਾਸਨ ਜਾਨੌ ਏਕ ਦਿਨ। ੨੩।","roman":"Ho beetai maas pachaasan jaanau ek din | 23 |","meaning_en":"though fifty months should pass, I shall count them as one day.","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਪੰਜਾਹ ਮਹੀਨੇ ਬੀਤਣ ਤੇ ਮੈਂ ਇਕ ਦਿਨ ਬੀਤਿਆ ਸਮਝਾਗੀ ॥੨੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[24],"number_text":"੨੪।","page":1839,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਚਕਿ ਮਚਕਿ ਕਬ ਕਹਿ ਹੈ ਬਚਨ ਬਨਾਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Machki machki kab kahi hai bachan banaai kai |","meaning_en":"When will he sway and sway and speak well-turned words?","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਉਹ ਮੈਨੂੰ) ਕਦ ਮਟਕ ਮਟਕ ਕੇ ਬੋਲ ਸੁਣਾਏਗਾ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਚਕਿ ਲਚਕਿ ਉਰ ਸਾਥ ਚਿਮਟਿ ਹੈ ਆਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Lachki lachki ur saath chimti hai aai kai |","meaning_en":"When will he come, bending gracefully, and cling to my breast?","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਤੇ ਲਚਕ ਲਚਕ ਕੇ ਮੇਰੇ ਹਿਰਦੇ ਨਾਲ ਆ ਕੇ ਚਿਮਟ ਜਾਏਗਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਪਟਿ ਲਪਟਿ ਮੈ ਜਾਉ ਪ੍ਰਿਯ ਕੈ ਅੰਗ ਤਨ।","roman":"Lapti lapti mai jaau priy kai ang tan |","meaning_en":"I shall cling and cling to the limbs and body of my dear one,","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮੈਂ ਵੀ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਮ ਦੇ ਸ਼ਰੀਰ ਨਾਲ ਲਿਪਟ ਲਿਪਟ ਜਾਵਾਗੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਮੇਲ ਮੇਲ ਕਰਿ ਰਾਖੋ ਭੀਤਰ ਤਾਹਿ ਮਨ। ੨੪।","roman":"Ho mel mel kari raakho bheetar taahi man | 24 |","meaning_en":"and keep him joined and joined within my heart.'","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਮੈ ਆਪਣਾ) ਮਨ ਉਸ ਦੇ ਅੰਦਰ ਮਿਲਾ ਮਿਲਾ ਕੇ ਰਖਾਗੀ ॥੨੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਵੈਯਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[25],"number_text":"੨੫।","page":1839,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਖੰਜਨ ਹੂੰ ਨ ਬਦ੍ਯੋ ਕਛੁ ਕੈ ਕਰਿ ਕੰਜੁ ਕੁਰੰਗ ਕਹਾ ਕਰਿ ਡਾਰੇ।","roman":"Khanjan hoon na badyo kachhu kai kari kanju kurang kahaa kari daare |","meaning_en":"'They count the wagtail as nothing at all; to what have they brought the lotus and the deer?","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"The queen praises the lover's eyes, comparing them with things eyes are usually likened to.","meaning_pa":"(ਮੈਂ ਤਾ ਹੁਣ) ਮਮੋਲੇ ਪੰਛੀ, ਕਮਲ ਅਤੇ ਹਿਰਨ ਨੂੰ ਵੀ ਕਿਧਰੋਂ ਦਾ ਕੁਝ ਨਹੀਂ ਸਮਝਦੀ ਹਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਾਰੁ ਚਕੋਰ ਨ ਆਨੇ ਹ੍ਰਿਦੈ ਪਰ ਝੁੰਡ ਝਖੀਨਹੁ ਕੋ ਝਝਕਾਰੇ।","roman":"Chaaru chakor na aane hridai par jhund jhakheenhu ko jhajhkaare |","meaning_en":"They do not take the lovely chakor to heart, and they have scorned whole shoals of fish.","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਝਝਕਾਰੇ: 'rebuffed'.","meaning_pa":"(ਹੁਣ) ਸੁੰਦਰ ਚਕੋਰ ਨੂੰ ਮੈਂ ਹਿਰਦੇ ਵਿਚ ਨਹੀਂ ਲਿਆਉਾਂਦੀ ਅਤੇ ਮੱਛੀਆਂ ਦੇ ਝੁੰਡ ਵੀ ਝਿੜਕ ਦਿੱਤੇ ਹਨ (ਅਰਥਾਤ ਸਮਾਨ ਨਹੀਂ ਮੰਨੇ ਹਨ)।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੈਨ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਮੁਰਛਾਇ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਲਖਿ ਸਾਰਸ ਭੈ ਸਭ ਦਾਸ ਬਿਚਾਰੇ।","roman":"Main rahiyo murchhaai prabhaa lakhi saaras bhai sabh daas bichaare |","meaning_en":"The god of love lies in a swoon at the sight of their radiance; the lotuses have all become poor slaves.","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਾਰਸ: 'lotus' (or 'crane'); uncertain."},{"gurmukhi":"ਅੰਤਕ ਸੋਚਨ ਧੀਰਜ ਮੋਚਨ ਲਾਲਚੀ ਲੋਚਨ ਲਾਲ ਤਿਹਾਰੇ। ੨੫।","roman":"Antak sochan dheeraj mochan laalchee lochan laal tihaare | 25 |","meaning_en":"Ending sorrow and taking away composure, your eyes, my darling, are greedy.'","page":1839,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅੰਤਕ ਸੋਚਨ: 'bringing an end to cares' or 'deadly, causing care'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"(ਉਸ ਦੀ) ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਕਾਮ ਦੇਵ ਮੂਰਛਿਤ ਹੋ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਸਾਰੇ ਸਾਰਸ ਵਿਚਾਰੇ ਦਾਸ ਹੋ ਗਏ ਹਨ। ਹੇ ਲਾਲ! ਤੇਰੇ ਲਾਲਚੀ ਨੈਣ ਚਿੰਤਾ ਨੂੰ ਖ਼ਤਮ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲੇ ਅਤੇ ਧੀਰਜ ਨੂੰ ਨਸ਼ਟ ਕਰਨ ਵਾਲੇ ਹਨ ॥੨੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB","note_pa":"ਇਹ ਅਰਥ ਇਸ ਪੰਕਤੀ ਸਮੇਤ ਉੱਪਰਲੀਆਂ 2 ਪੰਕਤੀਆਂ ਦਾ ਇਕੱਠਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਅੜਿਲ","gurmukhi":"ਅੜਿਲ","roman":"Aril","meaning_en":"Arril.","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੜਿਲ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[26],"number_text":"੨੬।","page":1841,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨਤ ਸਹਚਰੀ ਬਚਨ ਤਹਾ ਤੇ ਤਹ ਗਈ।","roman":"Sunat sahachree bachan tahaa te tah gaee |","meaning_en":"Hearing these words, the companion went from there to that place;","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਖੀ ਬੋਲ ਸੁਣ ਕੇ ਉਥੋਂ ਉਸ ਜਗ੍ਰਹਾ ਉਤੇ ਗਈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਾਤੁਰਤਾ ਬਹੁ ਭਾਤਿ ਸਿਖਾਵਤ ਇਹ ਭਈ।","roman":"Chaaturtaa bahu bhaati sikhaavat ih bhaee |","meaning_en":"she taught him cleverness in many ways.","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਬਹੁਤ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਦੀਆਂ ਚਾਲਾਕੀਆਂ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਸਿਖਾ ਦਿੱਤੀਆਂ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਸਤ੍ਰ ਮਲੀਨ ਉਤਾਰਿ ਭਲੇ ਪਹਿਰਾਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Basatr maleen utaari bhale pahiraai kai |","meaning_en":"Taking off his dirty clothes and dressing him in good ones,","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਉਸ ਦੇ) ਮੈਲੇ ਕਪੜੇ ਉਤਾਰ ਕੇ ਚੰਗੇ ਪਵਾ ਦਿੱਤੇ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਤਹ ਲ੍ਯਾਵਤ ਤਿਹ ਭਈ ਸੁ ਭੇਸ ਬਨਾਇ ਕੈ। ੨੬।","roman":"Ho tah lyaavat tih bhaee su bhes banaai kai | 26 |","meaning_en":"she brought him there, having made him handsomely attired.","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਦਾ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਰੂਪ ਬਣਾ ਕੇ ਉਥੇ ਲੈ ਆਈ ॥੨੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[27],"number_text":"੨੭।","page":1841,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਨ ਭਾਵਤ ਜਬ ਮੀਤ ਤਰੁਨਿ ਤਿਨ ਪਾਇਯੋ।","roman":"Man bhaavat jab meet taruni tin paaiyo |","meaning_en":"When the young woman got the friend her heart desired,","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਦ ਮਨ ਭਾਉਾਂਦਾ ਮਿਤਰ ਉਸ ਇਸਤਰੀ ਨੂੰ ਪ੍ਰਾਪਤ ਹੋ ਗਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਤਿ ਭਾਤਿ ਤਾ ਕੌ ਗਹਿ ਗਰੇ ਲਗਾਇਯੋ।","roman":"Bhaati bhaati taa kau gahi gare lagaaiyo |","meaning_en":"she took hold of him and held him to her neck in many ways.","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਕਈ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਨਾਲ ਪਕੜ ਕੇ ਗਲੇ ਨਾਲ ਲਗਾਇਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਸਨ ਚੁੰਬਨ ਕਰੇ ਹਰਖ ਉਪਜਾਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Aasan chunban kare harakh upjaai kai |","meaning_en":"She took postures and gave kisses, with joy rising in her,","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਪ੍ਰਸੰਨਤਾ ਪੂਰਵਕ ਉਸ ਨਾਲ ਆਸਣ ਅਤੇ ਚੁੰਬਨ ਕੀਤੇ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਤਵਨ ਸਖੀ ਕੋ ਦਾਰਿਦ ਸਕਲ ਮਿਟਾਇ ਕੈ। ੨੭।","roman":"Ho tavan sakhee ko daarid sakal mitaai kai | 27 |","meaning_en":"having wiped away all the poverty of that companion.","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"That is, she rewarded the maid richly.","meaning_pa":"(ਰਾਣੀ ਨੇ) ਉਸ ਸਖੀ ਦੀ ਸਾਰੀ ਗ਼ਰੀਬੀ ਖ਼ਤਮ ਕਰ ਦਿੱਤੀ ॥੨੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[28],"number_text":"੨੮।","page":1841,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦਿਜਿਕ ਦ੍ਰੁਗਾ ਕੀ ਪੂਜਾ ਕਰੀ ਰਿਝਾਇਯੋ।","roman":"Dijik drugaa kee poojaa karee rijhaaiyo |","meaning_en":"A Brahmin worshipped Durga and pleased her,","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦਿਜਿਕ: 'a Brahmin' (ਦਿਜ ਇਕ).","meaning_pa":"ਇਕ ਬ੍ਰਾਹਮਣ ਨੇ ਦੇਵੀ ਦੁਰਗਾ ਦੀ ਪੂਜਾ ਕਰ ਕੇ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਪ੍ਰਸੰਨ ਕਰ ਲਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਕੈ ਕਰ ਤੇ ਏਕ ਅਮਰ ਫਲ ਪਾਇਯੋ।","roman":"Taa kai kar te ek amar phal paaiyo |","meaning_en":"and from her hand received a fruit of immortality.","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਦੇ ਹੱਥ ਤੋਂ ਇਕ ਅਮਰ ਫਲ ਪ੍ਰਾਪਤ ਕੀਤਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਨਿ ਲੈ ਕੈ ਭਰਥਰਿ ਰਾਜਾ ਜੂ ਕੋ ਦਿਯੋ।","roman":"Tini lai kai bharathri raajaa joo ko diyo |","meaning_en":"He took it and gave it to King Bharthari:","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਫਲ ਲੈ ਕੇ (ਉਸ ਨੇ) ਰਾਜਾ ਭਰਥਰੀ ਨੂੰ ਦਿੱਤਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਜਬ ਲੌ ਪ੍ਰਿਥੀ ਅਕਾਸ ਨ੍ਰਿਪਤ ਤਬ ਲੌ ਜਿਯੋ। ੨੮।","roman":"Ho jab lau prithee akaas nripat tab lau jiyo | 28 |","meaning_en":"'As long as earth and sky last, so long may the king live.'","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਤਾ ਜੋ) ਜਦ ਤਕ ਪ੍ਰਿਥਵੀ ਅਤੇ ਆਕਾਸ਼ ਕਾਇਮ ਹਨ, ਉਦੋਂ ਤਕ ਰਾਜਾ ਜੀਉਾਂਦਾ ਰਹੇ ॥੨੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[29],"number_text":"੨੯।","page":1841,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਦੁਰਗ ਦਤ ਫਲ ਅਮਰ ਜਬੈ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਕਰ ਪਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Durag dat phal amar jabai nrip kar pariyo |","meaning_en":"When the immortal fruit given by Durga came into the king's hand,","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਦੋਂ ਦੁਰਗਾ ਦਾ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਹੋਇਆ ਫਲ ਰਾਜੇ ਦੇ ਹੱਥ ਪਿਆ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਨ ਮਤੀ ਕੋ ਦੇਉ ਇਹੈ ਚਿਤ ਮੈ ਕਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Bhaan matee ko deu ihai chit mai kariyo |","meaning_en":"he resolved in his mind, 'I will give it to Bhan Mati.'","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਾ ਮਨ ਵਿਚ ਇਹ ਸੋਚ ਕੇ (ਉਹ ਫਲ) ਭਾਨ ਮਤੀ ਨੂੰ ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ (ਕਿ ਇਹ ਚਿਰ ਤਕ ਜੀਵਿਤ ਰਹਿ ਕੇ ਸੇਵਾ ਕਰੇਗੀ)।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਰਿਯ ਕਿਯ ਮਨਹਿ ਬਿਚਾਰ ਕਿ ਮਿਤ੍ਰਹਿ ਦੀਜੀਯੈ।","roman":"Triy kiy manhi bichaar ki mitrahi deejeeyai |","meaning_en":"The woman thought in her mind, 'Let it be given to my friend;","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਇਸਤਰੀ ਨੇ ਮਨ ਵਿਚ ਵਿਚਾਰ ਕੀਤਾ (ਕਿ ਇਹ ਫਲ) ਮਿਤਰ ਨੂੰ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਜਾਵੇ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਸਦਾ ਤਰੁਨ ਸੋ ਰਹੈ ਕੇਲ ਅਤਿ ਕੀਜੀਯੈ। ੨੯।","roman":"Ho sadaa tarun so rahai kel ati keejeeyai | 29 |","meaning_en":"let him stay young for ever, and let there be much love-play.'","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜੋ ਸਦਾ ਜਵਾਨ ਰਹੇ ਅਤੇ (ਉਸ ਨਾਲ) ਬਹੁਤ ਕੇਲ-ਕ੍ਰੀੜਾ ਕਰਦਾ ਰਹੇ ॥੨੯॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[30],"number_text":"੩੦।","page":1841,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਨ ਭਾਵੰਤ ਮੀਤ ਜਦਿਨ ਸਖਿ ਪਾਈਯੈ।","roman":"Man bhaavant meet jadin sakhi paaeeyai |","meaning_en":"'On the day, O friend, that one finds the friend one's heart desires,","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹੇ ਸਖੀ! ਜਿਸ ਦਿਨ ਮਨ ਭਾਉਾਂਦਾ ਮਿਤਰ ਪ੍ਰਾਪਤ ਕਰ ਲਈਏ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਨ ਮਨ ਧਨ ਸਭ ਵਾਰਿ ਬਹੁਰੁ ਬਲਿ ਜਾਈਯੈ।","roman":"Tan man dhan sabh vaari bahuru bali jaaeeyai |","meaning_en":"one should offer up body, mind and wealth, and then be a sacrifice to him.","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਾ ਉਸ ਤੋਂ ਤਨ, ਮਨ ਅਤੇ ਧਨ ਸਭ ਕੁਝ ਵਾਰ ਕੇ ਫਿਰ ਬਲਿਹਾਰ ਜਾਣਾ ਚਾਹੀਦਾ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੋ ਮਨ ਲਯੋ ਚੁਰਾਇ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਮਹਿ ਆਜੁ ਸਭ।","roman":"Mo man layo churaai preetamhi aaju sabh |","meaning_en":"My beloved has today stolen my whole heart;","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਮੇਰੇ) ਪ੍ਰੀਤਮ ਨੇ ਅਜ ਮੇਰਾ ਮਨ ਸਭ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਨਾਲ ਚੁਰਾ ਲਿਆ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਰਹੈ ਤਰੁਨ ਚਿਰੁ ਜਿਯੈ ਦਿਯੌ ਫਲ ਤਾਹਿ ਲਭ। ੩੦।","roman":"Ho rahai tarun chiru jiyai diyau phal taahi labh | 30 |","meaning_en":"may he stay young and live long' - and she gave him the fruit that had been got.","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦਿਯੌ ਫਲ ਤਾਹਿ ਲਭ: 'gave him the fruit obtained'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਇਹ ਜਵਾਨ ਰਹੇ ਅਤੇ ਚਿਰ ਤਕ ਜੀਉਾਂਦਾ ਰਹੇ। (ਇਸ ਲਈ) ਫਲ ਲਭ ਕੇ (ਭਾਵ ਪ੍ਰਾਪਤ ਕਰ ਕੇ) ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ ॥੩੦॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[31],"number_text":"੩੧।","page":1841,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਕੋ ਚਿਤ ਰਾਨੀ ਹਰ ਲਯੋ। ਅਬਲਾ ਮਨੁ ਤਾ ਕੈ ਕਰ ਦਯੋ।","roman":"Nrip ko chit raanee har layo | ablaa manu taa kai kar dayo |","meaning_en":"The queen had taken away the king's heart; the woman gave her own heart into that man's hand.","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਜੇ ਦਾ ਚਿਤ ਰਾਣੀ ਨੇ ਹਰ ਲਿਆ। ਇਸਤਰੀ (ਰਾਣੀ) ਨੇ ਆਪਣਾ ਮਨ ਉਸ (ਚੰਡਾਲ) ਨੂੰ ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਵਹੁ ਅਟਕਤ ਬੇਸ੍ਵਾ ਪਰ ਭਯੋ। ਫਲ ਲੈ ਕੈ ਤਾ ਕੇ ਕਰ ਦਯੋ। ੩੧।","roman":"Vahu atkat besvaa par bhayo | phal lai kai taa ke kar dayo | 31 |","meaning_en":"He was caught up with a courtesan; taking the fruit, he gave it into her hand.","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬੇਸ੍ਵਾ: a courtesan.","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਅਗੋਂ ਇਕ ਵੇਸਵਾ ਉਤੇ ਅਟਕਿਆ ਹੋਇਆ ਸੀ। (ਉਸ ਨੇ ਉਹ) ਫਲ ਲੈ ਕੇ ਵੇਸਵਾ ਨੂੰ ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ ॥੩੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਅੜਿਲ","gurmukhi":"ਅੜਿਲ","roman":"Aril","meaning_en":"Arril.","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੜਿਲ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[32],"number_text":"੩੨।","page":1841,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰਹੀ ਤਰੁਨਿ ਸੋ ਰੀਝਿ ਅੰਗ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਕੇ ਨਿਰਖਿ।","roman":"Rahee taruni so reejhi ang nrip ke nirkhi |","meaning_en":"That young woman was charmed on seeing the limbs of the king;","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਇਸਤਰੀ (ਵੇਸਵਾ) ਰਾਜੇ ਦੇ ਸ਼ਰੀਰ (ਦੀ ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ) ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ (ਉਸ ਉਤੇ) ਰੀਝੀ ਹੋਈ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚਾਰੁ ਕੀਏ ਚਖ ਰਹੈ ਸਰੂਪ ਅਮੋਲ ਲਖਿ।","roman":"Chaaru kee'e chakh rahai saroop amol lakhi |","meaning_en":"she kept her lovely eyes on him, seeing his priceless form.","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਚਾਰੁ ਕੀਏ ਚਖ ਰਹੈ: 'kept her eyes made lovely'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਦੇ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਨੈਣ ਉਸ ਦੇ ਅਮੋਲਕ ਰੂਪ ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖਿਆ ਕਰਦੇ ਸਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਫਲ ਸੋਈ ਲੈ ਹਾਥ ਰੁਚਿਤ ਰੁਚਿ ਸੌ ਦਿਯੋ।","roman":"Phal soee lai haath ruchit ruchi sau diyo |","meaning_en":"Taking that same fruit in her hand, she gave it with eager liking:","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹੀ ਫਲ ਹੱਥ ਵਿਚ ਲੈ ਕੇ ਰੁਚੀ ਪੂਰਵਕ (ਰਾਜੇ ਨੂੰ) ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਜਬ ਲੌ ਪ੍ਰਿਥੀ ਅਕਾਸ ਨ੍ਰਿਪਤਿ ਤਬ ਲੌ ਜਿਯੋ। ੩੨।","roman":"Ho jab lau prithee akaas nripti tab lau jiyo | 32 |","meaning_en":"'As long as earth and sky last, so long may the king live.'","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿ ਜਦ ਤਕ ਪ੍ਰਿਥਵੀ ਅਤੇ ਆਕਾਸ਼ ਹਨ, ਰਾਜਾ ਉਦੋਂ ਤਕ ਜੀਵੇ ॥੩੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[33],"number_text":"੩੩।","page":1841,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਲੈ ਬੇਸ੍ਵਾ ਫਲ ਦਿਯੋ ਨ੍ਰਿਪਤਿ ਕੌ ਆਨਿ ਕੈ।","roman":"Lai besvaa phal diyo nripti kau aani kai |","meaning_en":"The courtesan took the fruit, brought it and gave it to the king;","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵੇਸਵਾ ਨੇ ਆ ਕੇ ਫਲ ਰਾਜੇ ਨੂੰ ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੂਪ ਹੇਰਿ ਬਸਿ ਭਈ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਅਤਿ ਠਾਨਿ ਕੈ।","roman":"Roop heri basi bhaee preeti ati thaani kai |","meaning_en":"seeing his beauty she had come under his sway, conceiving great love.","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਰਾਜੇ ਦਾ) ਰੂਪ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਅਤਿ ਅਧਿਕ ਪ੍ਰੀਤ ਕਾਰਨ ਉਸ ਦੇ ਵਸ ਵਿਚ ਹੋ ਗਈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲੈ ਰਾਜੈ ਤਿਹ ਹਾਥ ਚਿੰਤ ਚਿਤ ਮੈ ਕਿਯੋ।","roman":"Lai raajai tih haath chint chit mai kiyo |","meaning_en":"The king took it in his hand and reflected in his mind:","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਜੇ ਨੇ (ਫਲ) ਹੱਥ ਵਿਚ ਲੈ ਕੇ ਮਨ ਵਿਚ ਸੋਚ ਕੀਤੀ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਯਹ ਸੋਈ ਦ੍ਰੁਮ ਜਾਹਿ ਜੁ ਮੈ ਤ੍ਰਿਯ ਕੌ ਦਿਯੋ। ੩੩।","roman":"Ho yah soee drum jaahi ju mai triy kau diyo | 33 |","meaning_en":"'This is that very fruit which I gave to my wife.'","page":1841,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦ੍ਰੁਮ: 'tree', here the fruit of the tree; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਕਿ ਇਹ ਉਹੀ ਫਲ ('ਦ੍ਰੂਮ') ਹੈ ਜੋ ਮੈਂ ਇਸਤਰੀ (ਰਾਣੀ) ਨੂੰ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਸੀ ॥੩੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[34],"number_text":"੩੪।","page":1843,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਤਿ ਭਾਤਿ ਤਿਹ ਲੀਨੋ ਸੋਧ ਬਨਾਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Bhaati bhaati tih leeno sodh banaai kai |","meaning_en":"He examined it closely in many ways,","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਨੇ ਕਈ ਢੰਗਾ ਨਾਲ ਇਸ ਦੀ ਪੜਤਾਲ ਕੀਤੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਹ ਬੇਸ੍ਵਾ ਕੋ ਪੂਛ੍ਯੋ ਨਿਕਟਿ ਬੁਲਾਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Tih besvaa ko poochhyo nikti bulaai kai |","meaning_en":"and calling that courtesan near, he asked her:","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਵੇਸਵਾ ਨੂੰ ਕੋਲ ਬੁਲਾ ਕੇ ਪੁਛਿਆ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਾਚ ਕਹੋ ਮੁਹਿ ਯਹ ਫਲ ਤੈ ਕਹ ਤੇ ਲਹਿਯੋ।","roman":"Saach kaho muhi yah phal tai kah te lahiyo |","meaning_en":"'Tell me the truth: from where did you get this fruit?'","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮੈਨੂੰ ਸਚ ਦਸ, ਤੂੰ ਇਹ ਫਲ ਕਿਸ ਤੋਂ ਲਿਆ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਹਾਥ ਜੋਰਿ ਤਿਨ ਬਚਨ ਨ੍ਰਿਪਤਿ ਸੌ ਯੌ ਕਹਿਯੋ। ੩੪।","roman":"Ho haath jori tin bachan nripti sau yau kahiyo | 34 |","meaning_en":"Folding her hands, she spoke these words to the king:","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਨੇ ਹਥ ਜੋੜ ਕੇ ਰਾਜੇ ਨੂੰ ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਕਿਹਾ ॥੩੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[35],"number_text":"੩੫।","page":1843,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਮ ਅਪਨੇ ਚਿਤ ਜਿਹ ਰਾਨੀ ਕੇ ਕਰ ਦਿਯੋ।","roman":"Tum apne chit jih raanee ke kar diyo |","meaning_en":"'The queen into whose hand you gave it from your heart -","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਹੇ ਰਾਜਨ!) ਤੁਸੀਂ (ਜੋ ਫਲ) ਆਪਣੇ ਚਿਤ ਤੋਂ ਜਿਸ ਰਾਣੀ ਦੇ ਹੱਥ ਵਿਚ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਸੀ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਕੌ ਏਕ ਚੰਡਾਰ ਮੋਹਿ ਕਰਿ ਮਨੁ ਲਿਯੋ।","roman":"Taa kau ek chandaar mohi kari manu liyo |","meaning_en":"a chandal charmed her and took her heart.","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਰਾਣੀ ਦਾ ਮਨ ਇਕ ਚੰਡਾਲ ਨੇ ਮੋਹ ਲਿਆ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਵਨ ਨੀਚ ਮੁਹਿ ਊਪਰ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਬਿਕਾਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Tavan neech muhi oopar rahiyo bikaai kai |","meaning_en":"That low-born man has sold himself to me;","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਨੀਚ (ਚੰਡਾਲ) ਮੇਰੇ ਉਪਰ ਵੀ ਵਿਕਿਆ ਹੋਇਆ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਵ ਤ੍ਰਿਯ ਤਿਹ ਦਿਯ ਤਿਨ ਮੁਹਿ ਦਯੋ ਬਨਾਇ ਕੈ। ੩੫।","roman":"Tav triy tih diy tin muhi dayo banaai kai | 35 |","meaning_en":"your wife gave it to him, and he gave it to me.","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤੁਹਾਡੀ ਇਸਤਰੀ ਨੇ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਅਤੇ ਉਸ ਨੇ ਫਿਰ ਮੈਨੂੰ ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ ॥੩੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[36],"number_text":"੩੬।","page":1843,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੈ ਲਖਿ ਤੁਮਰੌ ਰੂਪ ਰਹੀ ਉਰਝਾਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Mai lakhi tumrau roop rahee urjhaai kai |","meaning_en":"Seeing your beauty, I have been caught fast;","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮੈਂ ਤੁਹਾਡਾ ਰੂਪ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਅਟਕੀ ਹੋਈ ਹਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਰਅਰਿ ਸਰ ਤਨ ਬਧੀ ਸੁ ਗਈ ਬਿਕਾਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Hara'ari sar tan badhee su gaee bikaai kai |","meaning_en":"pierced in the body by the arrows of Shiva's foe, I am sold to you.","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਹਰਅਰਿ: 'the enemy of Har (Shiva)', Kama.","meaning_pa":"ਸ਼ਿਵ ਦੇ ਵੈਰੀ ਕਾਮ ਦੇਵ ਦੇ ਬਾਣਾ ਨਾਲ ਵਿੰਨ੍ਰਹੀ ਹੋਈ (ਤੁਹਾਡੇ ਉਤੇ) ਵਿਕੀ ਹੋਈ ਹਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਦਾ ਤਰਨਿ ਤਾ ਕੋ ਫਲੁ ਹਮ ਤੇ ਲੀਜਿਯੈ।","roman":"Sadaa tarni taa ko phalu ham te leejiyai |","meaning_en":"Take from me this fruit of everlasting youth,","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਦਾ ਤਰਨਿ ਤਾ ਕੋ ਫਲੁ: 'the fruit of being ever young'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਸਦਾ ਜਵਾਨ ਰਖਣ ਵਾਲਾ ਇਹ ਫਲ ਮੇਰੇ ਤੋਂ ਲੈ ਲਵੋ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਕਾਮ ਕੇਲ ਮੁਹਿ ਸਾਥ ਹਰਖ ਸੋ ਕੀਜਿਯੈ। ੩੬।","roman":"Ho kaam kel muhi saath harakh so keejiyai | 36 |","meaning_en":"and make love with me joyfully.","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਤੇ ਮੇਰੇ ਨਾਲ ਪ੍ਰਸੰਨਤਾ ਪੂਰਵਕ ਕਾਮ-ਕ੍ਰੀੜਾ ਕਰੋ ॥੩੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[37],"number_text":"੩੭।","page":1843,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤੁਮ ਤਿਹ ਤ੍ਰਿਯ ਜੋ ਦਯੋ ਫਲ ਅਤਿ ਰੁਚਿ ਮਾਨਿ ਕੈ।","roman":"Tum tih triy jo dayo phal ati ruchi maani kai |","meaning_en":"The fruit that you gave to that woman with great liking,","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤੁਸੀਂ ਜੋ ਇਹ ਫਲ ਉਸ ਇਸਤਰੀ (ਰਾਣੀ) ਨੂੰ ਬਹੁਤ ਪ੍ਰਸੰਨ ਹੋ ਕੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਨ ਲੈ ਦਿਯੋ ਚੰਡਾਰਹਿ ਅਤਿ ਹਿਤੁ ਠਾਨਿ ਕੈ।","roman":"Tin lai diyo chandaarhi ati hitu thaani kai |","meaning_en":"she took and gave to the chandal with great affection;","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਨੇ ਚੰਡਾਲ ਨਾਲ ਪ੍ਰੀਤ ਪਾ ਕੇ (ਉਸ ਨੂੰ) ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਉਨ ਮੁਹਿ ਮੈ ਤੁਹਿ ਦਿਯੋ ਸੁ ਬਿਰਹਾ ਕੀ ਦਹੀ।","roman":"Un muhi mai tuhi diyo su birhaa kee dahee |","meaning_en":"he gave it to me, and I have given it to you, burned as I am by separation;","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ (ਚੰਡਾਲ ਨੇ ਫਲ) ਮੈਨੂੰ (ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ) ਅਤੇ ਮੈਂ ਵਿਯੋਗ ਦੀ ਸੜੀ ਹੋਈ ਨੇ ਤੁਹਾਨੂੰ ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਨਿਰਖਿ ਤਿਹਾਰੀ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਦਿਵਾਨੀ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਰਹੀ। ੩੭।","roman":"Ho nirkhi tihaaree prabhaa divaanee hvai rahee | 37 |","meaning_en":"seeing your radiance I have gone out of my mind.","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮੈਂ ਤੁਹਾਡੀ ਖ਼ੂਬਸੂਰਤੀ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਦੀਵਾਨੀ ਹੋ ਗਈ ਹਾ ॥੩੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[38],"number_text":"੩੮।","page":1843,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹੈ ਤਵ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਬਿਲੋਕਿ ਰਹੀ ਉਰਝਾਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Hai tav prabhaa biloki rahee urjhaai kai |","meaning_en":"Seeing your radiance I have been caught fast;","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਗ੍ਰਿਹ ਸਿਗਰੇ ਕੀ ਸੰਗ੍ਯਾ ਦਈ ਭੁਲਾਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Grih sigre kee sangyaa daee bhulaai kai |","meaning_en":"I have forgotten all awareness of my home.","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਅਮਰ ਅਜਰ ਫਲ ਤੁਮ ਕੌ ਦੀਨੋ ਆਨਿ ਕਰਿ।","roman":"Amar ajar phal tum kau deeno aani kari |","meaning_en":"I have brought and given you the undying, unageing fruit;","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮੈਂ ਤੁਹਾਡੀ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਮੋਹਿਤ ਹੋ ਗਈ ਹਾ। (ਮੈਂ) ਸਾਰੇ ਘਰ ਦੀ ਸੁੱਧ ਬੁੱਧ ਭੁਲਾ ਦਿੱਤੀ ਹੈ। (ਇਸ ਲਈ ਇਹ) ਅਮਰ ਅਜਰ ਫਲ ਤੁਹਾਨੂੰ ਲਿਆ ਕੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB","note_pa":"ਇਹ ਅਰਥ ਇਸ ਪੰਕਤੀ ਸਮੇਤ ਉੱਪਰਲੀਆਂ 3 ਪੰਕਤੀਆਂ ਦਾ ਇਕੱਠਾ ਹੈ।"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਤਾ ਤੇ ਮਦਨ ਸੰਤਾਪ ਨ੍ਰਿਪਤਿ ਹਮਰੋ ਪ੍ਰਹਰਿ। ੩੮।","roman":"Ho taa te madan santaap nripti hamro prahri | 38 |","meaning_en":"therefore, O king, take away the torment of love that is on me.'","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਇਸ ਲਈ) ਹੇ ਰਾਜਨ! ਮੇਰੀ ਕਾਮ-ਪੀੜਾ ਨੂੰ ਸੰਤੁਸ਼ਟ ਕਰੋ ॥੩੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[39],"number_text":"੩੯।","page":1843,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧੰਨ੍ਯ ਧੰਨ੍ਯ ਤਾ ਕੌ ਤਬ ਨ੍ਰਿਪਤਿ ਉਚਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Dhanny dhanny taa kau tab nripti uchaariyo |","meaning_en":"Then the king said to her, 'Blessed, blessed!'","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਦ ਰਾਜੇ ਨੇ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਧੰਨ ਧੰਨ ਕਿਹਾ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਤਿ ਭਾਤਿ ਸੌ ਤਾ ਕੇ ਸੰਗ ਬਿਹਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Bhaati bhaati sau taa ke sang bihaariyo |","meaning_en":"and took his pleasure with her in many ways.","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਤੇ ਭਾਤ ਭਾਤ ਨਾਲ ਉਸ ਨਾਲ ਰਮਣ ਕੀਤਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਪਟਿ ਲਪਟਿ ਬੇਸ੍ਵਾ ਹੂੰ ਗਈ ਬਨਾਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Lapti lapti besvaa hoon gaee banaai kai |","meaning_en":"The courtesan too clung and clung to him,","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵੇਸਵਾ ਵੀ ਉਸ ਨਾਲ ਚੰਗੀ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਲਿਪਟਦੀ ਗਈ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਅਪ੍ਰਮਾਨ ਦੁਤਿ ਹੇਰਿ ਰਹੀ ਉਰਝਾਇ ਕੈ। ੩੯।","roman":"Ho apramaan duti heri rahee urjhaai kai | 39 |","meaning_en":"caught fast at the sight of his measureless radiance.","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਤੇ ਉਸ ਦੀ ਅਨੂਪਮ ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਅਟਕ ਗਈ ॥੩੯॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[40],"number_text":"੪੦।","page":1843,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਨ ਭਾਵੰਤੋ ਮੀਤ ਜਵਨ ਦਿਨ ਪਾਈਯੈ।","roman":"Man bhaavanto meet javan din paaeeyai |","meaning_en":"On the day that one finds the friend one's heart desires,","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਸ ਦਿਨ ਮਨ ਭਾਉਾਂਦਾ ਮਿਤਰ ਪ੍ਰਾਪਤ ਹੋ ਜਾਏ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਵਨ ਘਰੀ ਕੇ ਪਲ ਪਲ ਬਲਿ ਬਲਿ ਜਾਈਯੈ।","roman":"Tavan gharee ke pal pal bali bali jaaeeyai |","meaning_en":"one should be a sacrifice to every instant of that hour,","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਾ ਉਸ ਘੜੀ ਦੇ ਪਲ ਪਲ ਤੋਂ ਵਾਰੇ ਵਾਰੇ ਜਾਈਏ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਲਪਟਿ ਲਪਟਿ ਕਰਿ ਤਾ ਸੌ ਅਧਿਕ ਬਿਹਾਰੀਯੈ।","roman":"Lapti lapti kari taa sau adhik bihaareeyai |","meaning_en":"cling and cling to him and take great pleasure with him,","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਲਿਪਟ ਲਿਪਟ ਕੇ ਉਸ ਨਾਲ ਅਧਿਕ ਰਮਣ ਕਰੀਏ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਤਤਖਿਨ ਦ੍ਰਪ ਕੰਦ੍ਰਪ ਕੋ ਸਕਲ ਨਿਵਾਰੀਯੈ। ੪੦।","roman":"Ho tatkhin drap kandrap ko sakal nivaareeyai | 40 |","meaning_en":"and at once put away all the pride of the god of love.","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦ੍ਰਪ ਕੰਦ੍ਰਪ ਕੋ: 'the pride of Kandarp (Kama)'.","meaning_pa":"ਅਤੇ ਉਸ ਛਿਣ ਕਾਮ ਦੇਵ ਦਾ ਸਾਰਾ ਘਮੰਡ ਦੂਰ ਕਰ ਦੇਈਏ ॥੪੦॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਵੈਯਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[41],"number_text":"੪੧।","page":1843,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਾਲ ਕੋ ਰੂਪ ਬਿਲੋਕਿ ਕੈ ਲਾਲ ਕਛੂ ਹਸਿ ਕੈ ਅਸ ਬੈਨ ਉਚਾਰੇ।","roman":"Baal ko roop biloki kai laal kachhoo hasi kai as bain uchaare |","meaning_en":"Seeing the beauty of the young woman, the dear one laughed a little and spoke these words:","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਲਾਲ: 'the dear one', the king.","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਜੇ ਨੇ ਵੇਸਵਾ ਦਾ ਰੂਪ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਅਤੇ ਹਸ ਕੇ ਕੁਝ ਬਚਨ ਉਚਾਰੇ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੈ ਅਟਕੀ ਸੁਨਿ ਸੁੰਦਰਿ ਮੋ ਪਰ ਐਸੇ ਨ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਅੰਗ ਹਮਾਰੇ।","roman":"Tai atkee suni sundri mo par aise na sundar ang hamaare |","meaning_en":"'Listen, beautiful one: you are caught on me, yet my limbs are not so beautiful.","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹੇ ਸੁੰਦਰੀ! ਸੁਣ, ਤੂੰ ਮੇਰੇ ਉਤੇ ਅਟਕੀ ਹੈਂ, ਪਰ ਮੇਰੇ ਇਤਨੇ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਅੰਗ ਤਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਹਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੀਬੋ ਘਨੋ ਸਿਗਰੋ ਜਗ ਚਾਹਤ ਸੋ ਨ ਰੁਚਿਯੋ ਚਿਤ ਮਾਝਿ ਤਿਹਾਰੇ।","roman":"Jeebo ghano sigro jag chaahat so na ruchiyo chit maajhi tihaare |","meaning_en":"The whole world wishes to live long, but that did not appeal to your heart.","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਾਰਾ ਜਗਤ ਬਹੁਤ ਜੀਉਣਾ ਚਾਹੁੰਦਾ ਹੈ, ਪਰ ਇਹ ਗੱਲ ਤੇਰੇ ਚਿਤ ਨੂੰ ਕਿਉਾਂ ਨਾ ਚੰਗੀ ਲਗੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਆਨਿ ਜਰਾਰਿ ਦਯੋ ਹਮ ਕੌ ਫਲੁ ਦਾਸ ਭਏ ਹਮ ਆਜੁ ਤਿਹਾਰੇ। ੪੧।","roman":"Aani jaraari dayo ham kau phalu daas bhae ham aaju tihaare | 41 |","meaning_en":"You have brought and given me the fruit that defeats old age; today I have become your slave.'","page":1843,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜਰਾਰਿ: 'the enemy of old age'.","meaning_pa":"ਇਹ ਬੁਢਾਪੇ ਦਾ ਵੈਰੀ ਜਾ ਅਮਰ ('ਜਰਾਰਿ') ਫਲ ਮੈਨੂੰ ਆਣ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਹੈ। ਇਸ ਲਈ ਅਜ ਮੈਂ ਤੇਰਾ ਦਾਸ ਹੋ ਗਿਆ ਹਾ ॥੪੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਬੇਸ੍ਵਾ ਵਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਬੇਸ੍ਵਾ ਵਾਚ","roman":"Besvaa vaach","meaning_en":"The courtesan said:","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਵੇਸਵਾ ਨੇ ਕਿਹਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[42],"number_text":"੪੨।","page":1845,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨੈਨ ਲਗੇ ਜਬ ਤੇ ਤੁਮ ਸੌ ਤਬ ਤੇ ਤਵ ਹੇਰਿ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਬਲਿ ਜਾਊ।","roman":"Nain lage jab te tum sau tab te tav heri prabhaa bali jaaoo |","meaning_en":"'Ever since my eyes met yours, I have been a sacrifice to the sight of your radiance.","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਹੇ ਰਾਜਨ!) ਸੁਣੋ, ਜਦ ਦੀਆਂ ਤੁਹਾਡੇ ਨਾਲ ਅੱਖਾ ਲਗੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਉਦੋਂ ਤੋਂ ਤੁਹਾਡੀ ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਬਲਿਹਾਰੀ ਜਾ ਰਹੀ ਹਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭੌਨ ਭੰਡਾਰ ਸੁਹੁਾਤ ਨ ਮੋ ਕਹ ਸੋਵਤ ਹੂੰ ਬਿਝ ਕੈ ਬਰਰਾਊ।","roman":"Bhaun bhandaar suhaat na mo kah sovat hoon bijh kai barraaoo |","meaning_en":"House and treasury do not please me; even in sleep I start up and babble.","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬਿਝ ਕੈ: 'starting up'; uncertain. ਸੁਹੁਾਤ: printed so.","meaning_pa":"ਮਹੱਲ ਅਤੇ ਭੰਡਾਰ ਮੈਨੂੰ ਚੰਗੇ ਨਹੀਂ ਲਗਦੇ ਅਤੇ ਸੁੱਤੀ ਹੋਈ ਚੌਂਕ ਕੇ ਬਰੜਾਉਣ ਲਗਦੀ ਹਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੈਤਿਕ ਆਪਨੀ ਆਰਬਲਾ ਸਭ ਮੀਤ ਕੇ ਊਪਰ ਵਾਰਿ ਬਹਾਊ।","roman":"Jaitik aapnee aarablaa sabh meet ke oopar vaari bahaaoo |","meaning_en":"Whatever span of life is mine, I would offer it all over my friend and cast it away.","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਆਰਬਲਾ: span of life."},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੇਤਿਕ ਬਾਤ ਜਰਾਰਿ ਸੁਨੋ ਫਲ ਪ੍ਰਾਨ ਦੈ ਮੋਲ ਪਿਯਾ ਕਹ ਲ੍ਯਾਊ। ੪੨।","roman":"Ketik baat jaraari suno phal praan dai mol piyaa kah lyaaoo | 42 |","meaning_en":"Listen: what is a fruit that defeats old age? I would buy my beloved at the price of my life.","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਮੇਰੀ) ਜਿਤਨੀ ਵੀ ਆਯੂ ਹੈ, ਸਾਰੀ ਮਿਤਰ ਉਪਰੋਂ ਵਾਰ ਦੇਣਾ ਚਾਹੁੰਦੀ ਹਾ। ਅਮਰ ('ਜਰਾਰਿ') ਫਲ ਦੀ ਕੀ ਗੱਲ ਹੈ, ਮੈਂ ਤਾ ਪ੍ਰਾਣਾ ਦਾ ਮੁੱਲ ਤਾਰ ਕੇ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਮ ਨੂੰ ਪ੍ਰਾਪਤ ਕਰ ਲਵਾਗੀ ॥੪੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB","note_pa":"ਇਹ ਅਰਥ ਇਸ ਪੰਕਤੀ ਸਮੇਤ ਉੱਪਰਲੀਆਂ 2 ਪੰਕਤੀਆਂ ਦਾ ਇਕੱਠਾ ਹੈ।"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[43],"number_text":"੪੩।","page":1845,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਤੈ ਜੁ ਦਿਯੋ ਤੀਯ ਕੋ ਫਲ ਥੋ ਦਿਜ ਤੇ ਕਰਿ ਕੋਟਿਕੁਪਾਇ ਲੀਯੋ।","roman":"Tai ju diyo teey ko phal tho dij te kari kotikupaai leeyo |","meaning_en":"The fruit that you gave your wife, which was got from the Brahmin by countless efforts,","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕੋਟਿਕੁਪਾਇ: 'by crores of means'.","meaning_pa":"ਤੁਸੀਂ ਜੋ ਫਲ ਇਸਤਰੀ (ਰਾਣੀ) ਨੂੰ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਸੀ, ਉਹ ਬ੍ਰਾਹਮਣ ਨੇ ਬਹੁਤ ਉਪਾ ਕਰ ਕੇ ਪ੍ਰਾਪਤ ਕੀਤਾ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੋਊ ਲੈ ਕਰ ਜਾਰ ਕੌ ਦੇਤ ਭਈ ਤਿਨ ਰੀਝਿ ਕੈ ਮੋ ਪਰ ਮੋਹਿ ਦੀਯੋ।","roman":"So'oo lai kar jaar kau det bhaee tin reejhi kai mo par mohi deeyo |","meaning_en":"she took and gave to her lover, and he, pleased with me, gave it to me.","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਲੈ ਕੇ (ਰਾਣੀ ਨੇ) ਯਾਰ ਨੂੰ ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਅਤੇ ਉਸ (ਯਾਰ) ਨੇ ਪ੍ਰਸੰਨ ਹੋ ਕੇ ਮੈਨੂੰ ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਹੌ ਅਟਕੀ ਤਵ ਹੇਰਿ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਤਨ ਕੋ ਤਨਿ ਕੈ ਨਹਿ ਤਾਪ ਕੀਯੋ।","roman":"Nrip hau atkee tav heri prabhaa tan ko tani kai nahi taap keeyo |","meaning_en":"O king, I was caught at the sight of your radiance, and did not care in the least for my body's own pain.","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤਨ ਕੋ ਤਨਿ ਕੈ ਨਹਿ ਤਾਪ ਕੀਯੋ: sense uncertain; read as 'did not mind my body's suffering even a little'.","meaning_pa":"ਹੇ ਰਾਜਨ! ਤੇਰੇ ਸ਼ਰੀਰ ਦੀ ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਮੈਂ ਅਟਕ ਗਈ ਹਾ, (ਇਸ ਲਈ ਮੈਨੂੰ ਫਲ ਦਿੰਦਿਆਂ) ਕੋਈ ਦੁਖ ਨਹੀਂ ਹੋਇਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਹ ਖਾਹੁ ਹਮੈ ਸੁਖ ਦੇਹ ਦਿਯੋ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਰਾਜ ਕਰੋ ਜੁਗ ਚਾਰ ਜੀਯੋ। ੪੩।","roman":"Tih khaahu hamai sukh deh diyo nrip raaj karo jug chaar jeeyo | 43 |","meaning_en":"Eat it, give me the pleasure of your body, O king; rule and live for the four ages.'","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁਖ ਦੇਹ ਦਿਯੋ: read as 'give bodily pleasure'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"(ਤੁਸੀਂ) ਇਸ ਫਲ ਨੂੰ ਖਾਓ, ਮੈਨੂੰ ਦੇਹ ਦਾ ਸੁਖ ਦਿਓ ਅਤੇ ਹੇ ਰਾਜਾ ਜੀ! (ਤੁਸੀਂ) ਚਾਰ ਯੁਗਾ ਤਕ ਰਾਜ ਕਰੋ ॥੪੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਭਰਥਰਿ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਭਰਥਰਿ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Bharathri baach","meaning_en":"Bharthari said:","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਭਰਥਰੀ ਨੇ ਕਿਹਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਅੜਿਲ","gurmukhi":"ਅੜਿਲ","roman":"Aril","meaning_en":"Arril.","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੜਿਲ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[44],"number_text":"੪੪।","page":1845,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਧ੍ਰਿੰਗ ਮੁਹਿ ਕੌ ਮੈ ਜੁ ਫਲੁ ਤ੍ਰਿਯਹਿ ਦੈ ਡਾਰਿਯੌ।","roman":"Dhring muhi kau mai ju phalu triyhi dai daariyau |","meaning_en":"'Shame on me, that I gave the fruit away to my wife.","page":1845,"flags":[{"code":"0x71","reason":"subjoined letter typed after the vowel/nasal sign; put in Unicode order (same printed shape)"}],"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮੈਨੂੰ ਧਿੱਕਾਰ ਹੈ ਜੋ ਉਹ ਫਲ ਇਸਤਰੀ (ਰਾਣੀ) ਨੂੰ ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧ੍ਰਿਗ ਤਿਹ ਦਿਯੋ ਚੰਡਾਰ ਜੁ ਧ੍ਰਮ ਨ ਬਿਚਾਰਿਯੌ।","roman":"Dhrig tih diyo chandaar ju dhram na bichaariyau |","meaning_en":"Shame on her who gave it to the chandal and did not think of righteousness.","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ (ਰਾਣੀ) ਨੂੰ ਵੀ ਧਿੱਕਾਰ ਹੈ (ਜਿਸ ਨੇ ਇਹ ਫਲ) ਧਰਮ ਨੂੰ ਵਿਚਾਰੇ ਬਿਨਾ ਚੰਡਾਲ ਨੂੰ ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਧ੍ਰਿਗ ਤਾ ਕੋ ਤਿਨ ਤ੍ਰਿਯ ਰਾਨੀ ਸੀ ਪਾਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Dhrig taa ko tin triy raanee see paai kai |","meaning_en":"Shame on him who, having gained a woman like the queen,","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਉਸ (ਚੰਡਾਲ) ਨੂੰ ਵੀ ਧਿੱਕਾਰ ਹੈ ਜਿਸ ਨੇ ਰਾਣੀ ਵਰਗੀ ਇਸਤਰੀ ਪ੍ਰਾਪਤ ਕਰ ਕੇ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਦਯੋ ਬੇਸ੍ਵਹਿ ਪਰਮ ਪ੍ਰੀਤਿ ਉਪਜਾਇ ਕੈ। ੪੪।","roman":"Ho dayo besvahi param preeti upjaai kai | 44 |","meaning_en":"gave it to a courtesan, conceiving great love for her.'","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਉਹ ਫਲ) ਇਕ ਵੇਸਵਾ ਨਾਲ ਬਹੁਤ ਪ੍ਰੀਤ ਪੈਦਾ ਕਰ ਕੇ ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ ॥੪੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਵੈਯਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[45],"number_text":"੪੫।","page":1845,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਆਧਿਕ ਆਪੁ ਭਖ੍ਯੋ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਲੈ ਫਲ ਆਧਿਕ ਰੂਪਮਤੀ ਕਹ ਦੀਨੋ।","roman":"Aadhik aapu bhakhyo nrip lai phal aadhik roopamtee kah deeno |","meaning_en":"The king took the fruit and ate half himself, and half he gave to Rupmati.","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰੂਪਮਤੀ: 'the beautiful one'; taken as the courtesan's name; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਜੇ ਨੇ ਫਲ ਲੈ ਕੇ ਅੱਧਾ ਆਪ ਖਾਇਆ ਅਤੇ ਅੱਧਾ ਰੂਪਮਤੀ (ਵੇਸਵਾ) ਨੂੰ ਦੇ ਦਿੱਤਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਯਾਰ ਕੈ ਟੂਕ ਹਜਾਰ ਕਰੇ ਗਹਿ ਨਾਰਿ ਭਿਟ੍ਯਾਰ ਤਿਨੈ ਬਧਿ ਕੀਨੋ।","roman":"Yaar kai took hajaar kare gahi naari bhityaar tinai badhi keeno |","meaning_en":"He cut the lover into a thousand pieces, and seizing the wife and the go-between, he killed them.","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਿਟ੍ਯਾਰ: unclear; read as the woman who brought them together (the maid); uncertain.","meaning_pa":"(ਉਸ) ਯਾਰ (ਚੰਡਾਲ) ਦੇ ਹਜ਼ਾਰ ਟੋਟੇ ਕਰ ਦਿੱਤੇ ਅਤੇ ਰਾਣੀ ਤੇ ਦਾਸੀ ('ਭਿਟ੍ਰਯਾਰ' ਰਾਣੀ ਦਾ ਚੰਡਾਲ ਨਾਲ ਮੇਲ ਕਰਾਉਣ ਵਾਲੀ) ਨੂੰ ਮਾਰ ਦਿੱਤਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭੌਨ ਭੰਡਾਰ ਬਿਸਾਰ ਸਭੈ ਕਛੁ ਰਾਮ ਕੋ ਨਾਮੁ ਹ੍ਰਿਦੈ ਦ੍ਰਿੜ ਚੀਨੋ।","roman":"Bhaun bhandaar bisaar sabhai kachhu raam ko naamu hridai drir cheeno |","meaning_en":"Forgetting house, treasury and all else, he fixed the Name of Ram firmly in his heart.","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਮਹੱਲ, ਖ਼ਜ਼ਾਨੇ ਅਤੇ ਹੋਰ ਸਭ ਕੁਝ ਵਿਸਾਰ ਕੇ ਰਾਮ ਨਾਮ ਨੂੰ ਹਿਰਦੇ ਵਿਚ ਦ੍ਰਿੜ੍ਰਹ ਕਰ ਲਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਾਇ ਬਸ੍ਯੋ ਤਬ ਹੀ ਬਨ ਮੈ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਭੇਸ ਕੋ ਤ੍ਯਾਗ ਜੁਗੇਸ ਕੋ ਲੀਨੋ। ੪੫।","roman":"Jaai basyo tab hee ban mai nrip bhes ko tyaag juges ko leeno | 45 |","meaning_en":"He went at once and lived in the forest; giving up the dress of a king, he took that of a lord of yogis.","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਭਰਥਰੀ ਨੇ) ਰਾਜੇ ਵਾਲੇ ਬਸਤ੍ਰ ਤਿਆਗ ਕੇ ਜੋਗੀ ਵਾਲਾ ਭੇਖ ਕਰ ਲਿਆ ਅਤੇ ਬਨ ਵਿਚ ਜਾ ਟਿਕਿਆ ॥੪੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[46],"number_text":"੪੬।","page":1845,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬਨ ਭੀਤਰ ਭੇਟਾ ਭਈ ਗੋਰਖ ਸੰਗ ਸੁ ਧਾਰ।","roman":"Ban bheetar bhetaa bhaee gorakh sang su dhaar |","meaning_en":"In the forest he met with Gorakh;","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸੁ ਧਾਰ: filler for the rhyme, 'well'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"(ਰਾਜੇ ਦੀ) ਬਨ ਵਿਚ ਗੋਰਖਨਾਥ ਨਾਲ ਭੇਾਂਟ ਹੋਈ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰਾਜ ਤ੍ਯਾਗ ਅੰਮ੍ਰਿਤ ਲਯੋ ਭਰਥਿਰ ਰਾਜ ਕੁਮਾਰ। ੪੬।","roman":"Raaj tyaag anmrit layo bharthir raaj kumaar | 46 |","meaning_en":"giving up his kingdom, the prince Bharthari took the nectar of immortality.","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅੰਮ੍ਰਿਤ: nectar; the yogic teaching is meant.","meaning_pa":"ਅਤੇ ਰਾਜ-ਪਾਟ ਤਿਆਗ ਕੇ ਭਰਥਰੀ ਰਾਜ ਕੁਮਾਰ ਨੇ ਅੰਮ੍ਰਿਤ ਪ੍ਰਾਪਤ ਕੀਤਾ ॥੪੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸਵੈਯਾ","roman":"Savaiyaa","meaning_en":"Savaiya.","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸਵੈਯਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[47],"number_text":"੪੭।","page":1845,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਰੋਵਤ ਹੈ ਸੁ ਕਹੂੰ ਪੁਰ ਕੇ ਜਨ ਬੌਰੇ ਸੇ ਡੋਲਤ ਜ੍ਯੋ ਮਤਵਾਰੇ।","roman":"Rovat hai su kahoon pur ke jan baure se dolat jyo matvaare |","meaning_en":"Somewhere the people of the city weep, and wander about like madmen or drunkards;","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਨਗਰ ਦੇ ਲੋਕ ਰੋਂਦੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਬੌਰਿਆਂ ਵਾਗ ਮਤਵਾਲੇ ਹੋਏ ਡੋਲਦੇ ਫਿਰਦੇ ਹਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਫਾਰਤ ਚੀਰ ਸੁ ਬੀਰ ਗਿਰੇ ਕਹੂੰ ਜੂਝੈ ਹੈ ਖੇਤ ਮਨੋ ਜੁਝਿਯਾਰੇ।","roman":"Phaarat cheer su beer gire kahoon joojhai hai khet mano jujhiyaare |","meaning_en":"somewhere brave men have fallen, tearing their clothes, as if warriors had fallen on the field;","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਸੂਰਮੇ ਬਸਤ੍ਰ ਪਾੜ ਕੇ ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਡਿਗੇ ਪਏ ਹਨ, ਮਾਨੋ ਯੁੱਧ-ਭੂਮੀ ਵਿਚ ਯੋਧੇ ਜੂਝੇ ਪਏ ਹੋਣ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਰੋਵਤ ਨਾਰ ਅਪਾਰ ਕਹੂੰ ਬਿਸੰਭਾਰਿ ਭਈ ਕਰਿ ਨੈਨਨ ਤਾਰੇ।","roman":"Rovat naar apaar kahoon bisanbhaari bhaee kari nainan taare |","meaning_en":"somewhere countless women weep, and have lost their senses with their eyes fixed and staring:","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਰਿ ਨੈਨਨ ਤਾਰੇ: 'with the pupils of the eyes fixed'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ ਬੇਸ਼ੁਮਾਰ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਰੋ ਰਹੀਆਂ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਬਿਨਾ ਨੈਣ ਝਮਕਾਏ ਬੇਹੋਸ਼ ਪਈਆਂ ਹਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਯਾਗ ਕੈ ਰਾਜ ਸਮਾਜ ਸਭੈ ਮਹਾਰਾਜ ਸਖੀ ਬਨ ਆਜੁ ਪਧਾਰੇ। ੪੭।","roman":"Tyaag kai raaj samaaj sabhai mahaaraaj sakhee ban aaju padhaare | 47 |","meaning_en":"'Giving up all his royal state, O friend, the great king has gone to the forest today.'","page":1845,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਅਤੇ ਕਹਿੰਦੀਆਂ ਫਿਰਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ) ਹੇ ਸਖੀ! ਸਾਰੇ ਰਾਜ-ਪਾਟ ਨੂੰ ਛਡ ਕੇ ਮਹਾਰਾਜ ਅਜ ਬਨ ਨੂੰ ਚਲੇ ਗਏ ਹਨ ॥੪੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[48],"number_text":"੪੮।","page":1847,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਨਿਜੁ ਨਾਰਿ ਨਿਹਾਰਿ ਕੈ ਭਰਥ ਕੁਮਾਰਿ ਬਿਸਾਰਿ ਸੰਭਾਰਿ ਛਕੀ ਮਨ ਮੈ।","roman":"Niju naari nihaari kai bharath kumaari bisaari sanbhaari chhakee man mai |","meaning_en":"His own wives, on seeing Prince Bharthari, lost all composure and were dazed in mind.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਭਰਥ ਕੁਮਾਰਿ: read as 'Prince Bharthari' (ਕੁਮਾਰ); uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਭਰਥਰੀ ਕੁਮਾਰ ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖ ਕੇ ਉਸ ਦੀਆਂ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਹੋਸ਼ ਭੁਲਾ ਕੇ ਮਨ ਵਿਚ (ਦੁਖ ਨਾਲ) ਭਰੀਆਂ ਪਈਆਂ ਹਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਹੂੰ ਹਾਰ ਗਿਰੈ ਕਹੂੰ ਬਾਰ ਲਸੈ ਕਛੁ ਨੈਕੁ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਨ ਰਹੀ ਤਨ ਮੈ।","roman":"Kahoon haar girai kahoon baar lasai kachhu naiku prabhaa na rahee tan mai |","meaning_en":"Here a necklace falls, there the hair hangs loose; not the least lustre is left in their bodies.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿਤੇ (ਉਨ੍ਰਹਾ ਦੇ) ਹਾਰ ਡਿਗੇ ਪਏ ਹਨ, ਕਿਤੇ ਵਾਲ (ਖਿਲਰੇ ਹੋਏ) ਲਿਸ਼ਕ ਰਹੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ (ਕਿਸੇ ਦੇ) ਤਨ ਵਿਚ ਜ਼ਰਾ ਜਿੰਨੀ ਵੀ ਸ਼ੋਭਾ ਨਹੀਂ ਰਹੀ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਝਖ ਕੇਤੁਕ ਬਾਨਨ ਪੀੜਤ ਭੀ ਮਨ ਜਾਇ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਮਨ ਮੋਹਨ ਮੈ।","roman":"Jhakh ketuk baanan peerat bhee man jaai rahiyo man mohan mai |","meaning_en":"They were tormented by the arrows of the fish-bannered god; their minds had gone and stayed with the charmer of their hearts,","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਝਖ ਕੇਤੁ: Kama, whose banner bears a fish.","meaning_pa":"ਕਈ ਕਾਮ ਦੇਵ ('ਝਖ ਕੇਤੁ') ਦੇ ਬਾਣ ਲਗਣ ਨਾਲ ਦੁਖੀ ਹੋ ਗਈਆਂ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਉਨ੍ਰਹਾ ਦਾ ਮਨ ਮਨਮੋਹਨ ਪਾਸ ਚਲਾ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮਨੋ ਦੀਪਕ ਭੇਦ ਸੁਨੋ ਸੁਰ ਨਾਦ ਮ੍ਰਿਗੀ ਗਨ ਜਾਨੁ ਬਿਧੀ ਮਨ ਮੈ। ੪੮।","roman":"Mano deepak bhed suno sur naad mrigee gan jaanu bidhee man mai | 48 |","meaning_en":"as if a herd of does, hearing the notes of the Dipak raga, had been pierced in the heart.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਦੀਪਕ ਭੇਦ: 'a mode of Dipak', the raga; the line is compressed; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"(ਇੰਜ ਪ੍ਰਤੀਤ ਹੁੰਦਾ ਹੈ) ਮਾਨੋ ਦੀਪਕ ਦਾ ਭੇਦ (ਪਰਵਾਨਿਆਂ ਨੇ ਪਾ ਲਿਆ ਹੋਵੇ) ਜਾ ਮਾਨੋ ਘੰਡਾ ਹੇੜੇ ਦਾ ਨਾਦ ਸੁਣ ਕੇ ਬਹੁਤ ਸਾਰੀਆਂ ਹਿਰਨੀਆਂ ਮਨ ਵਿਚ ਵਿੰਨ੍ਰਹੀਆਂ ਗਈਆਂ ਹੋਣ ॥੪੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[49],"number_text":"੪੯।","page":1847,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਨਿਕ ਜਤਨ ਕਰਿ ਕਰਿ ਤ੍ਰਿਯਾ ਹਾਰਤ ਭਈ ਅਨੇਕ।","roman":"Anik jatan kari kari triyaa haarat bhaee anek |","meaning_en":"The many women wore themselves out with countless efforts;","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਨੇਕਾ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਕਈ ਪ੍ਰਕਾਰ ਦੇ ਯਤਨ ਕਰ ਕਰ ਕੇ ਹਾਰ ਗਈਆਂ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਨ ਹੀ ਕੌ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਜਾਤ ਭਯੋ ਮਾਨਿਯੋ ਬਚਨ ਨ ਏਕ। ੪੯।","roman":"Ban hee kau nrip jaat bhayo maaniyo bachan na ek | 49 |","meaning_en":"the king went away to the forest and did not heed a single word.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਪਰ ਰਾਜਾ ਬਨ ਨੂੰ ਚਲਾ ਗਿਆ ਅਤੇ ਕਿਸੇ ਇਕ ਦੀ ਵੀ ਗੱਲ ਨਾ ਮੰਨੀ ॥੪੯॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[50],"number_text":"੫੦।","page":1847,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜਬ ਰਾਜਾ ਬਨ ਮੈ ਗਏ ਗੋਰਖ ਗੁਰੂ ਬੁਲਾਇ।","roman":"Jab raajaa ban mai gae gorakh guroo bulaai |","meaning_en":"When the king had gone into the forest, Guru Gorakh called him,","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਦ ਰਾਜਾ ਬਨ ਵਿਚ ਗਿਆ (ਤਾ) ਗੁਰੂ ਗੋਰਖ ਨਾਥ ਨੇ ਬੁਲਾ ਲਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਹੁਰਿ ਭਾਤਿ ਸਿਛ੍ਯਾ ਦਈ ਤਾਹਿ ਸਿਖ੍ਯ ਠਹਰਾਇ। ੫੦।","roman":"Bahuri bhaati sichhyaa daee taahi sikhy thahraai | 50 |","meaning_en":"and making him his disciple, gave him teaching in many ways.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਈ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਦੀ ਸਿਖਿਆ ਦੇ ਕੇ ਉਸ ਨੂੰ ਆਪਣਾ ਚੇਲਾ ਬਣਾ ਲਿਆ ॥੫੦॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਭਰਥਰੀ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਭਰਥਰੀ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Bharathree baach","meaning_en":"Bharthari said:","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਭਰਥਰੀ ਨੇ ਕਿਹਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[51],"number_text":"੫੧।","page":1847,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਵਨ ਮਰੈ ਮਾਰੈ ਕਵਨ ਕਹਤ ਸੁਨਤ ਕਹ ਕੋਇ।","roman":"Kavan marai maarai kavan kahat sunat kah koi |","meaning_en":"'Who dies and who kills? Who is it that speaks and hears?","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਹੇ ਗੁਰੂ ਗੋਰਖ ਨਾਥ! ਇਹ ਦਸੋ) ਕੌਣ ਮਰਦਾ ਹੈ, ਕੌਣ ਮਾਰਦਾ ਹੈ, ਕੌਣ ਕਹਿੰਦਾ ਹੈ, ਕੌਣ ਸੁਣਦਾ ਹੈ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੋ ਰੋਵੈ ਕਵਨੈ ਹਸੈ ਕਵਨ ਜਰਾ ਜਿਤ ਹੋਇ। ੫੧।","roman":"Ko rovai kavnai hasai kavan jaraa jit hoi | 51 |","meaning_en":"Who weeps and who laughs? Who is overcome by old age?'","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਵਨ ਜਰਾ ਜਿਤ ਹੋਇ: 'who becomes conquered by age' (or 'conquers age'); uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਕੌਣ ਰੋਂਦਾ ਹੈ, ਕੌਣ ਹਸਦਾ ਹੈ, ਕੌਣ ਬੁਢਾਪੇ ਨੂੰ ਜਿਤਣ ਵਾਲਾ ਹੈ? ॥੫੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[52],"number_text":"੫੨।","page":1847,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਹਸਿ ਗੋਰਖ ਇਮਿ ਬਚਨ ਉਚਾਰੇ। ਸੁਨਹੁ ਭਰਥ ਹਰਿ ਰਾਜ ਹਮਾਰੇ।","roman":"Hasi gorakh imi bachan uchaare | sunhu bharath hari raaj hamaare |","meaning_en":"Laughing, Gorakh spoke these words: 'Listen, Bharthari, my king.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਗੋਰਖ ਨੇ ਹਸ ਕੇ ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਕਿਹਾ, ਹੇ ਮੇਰੇ ਭਰਥਰੀ ਹਰਿ ਰਾਜਾ! ਸੁਣੋ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਤਿ ਝੂਠ ਮੂਓ ਹੰਕਾਰਾ। ਕਬਹੂ ਮਰਤ ਨ ਬੋਲਨਹਾਰਾ। ੫੨।","roman":"Sati jhooth moo'o hankaaraa | kabhoo marat na bolanhaaraa | 52 |","meaning_en":"Truth, falsehood and pride die; the one who speaks never dies.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਬੋਲਨਹਾਰਾ: 'the speaker', the soul within. ਸਤਿ ਝੂਠ: 'truth and falsehood'; could also be read 'truly, falsehood and pride die'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਸਚ, ਝੂਠ ਅਤੇ ਹੰਕਾਰ ਮਰਦਾ ਹੈ, ਪਰ ਬੋਲਣ ਵਾਲੀ ਆਤਮਾ ਕਦੇ ਵੀ ਨਹੀਂ ਮਰਦੀ ॥੫੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[53],"number_text":"੫੩।","page":1847,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਲ ਮਰੈ ਕਾਯਾ ਮਰੈ ਕਾਲੈ ਕਰਤ ਉਚਾਰ।","roman":"Kaal marai kaayaa marai kaalai karat uchaar |","meaning_en":"It is Kal that dies, the body that dies, and Kal that utters speech;","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਾਲ: Time/Death, here the power working in all; left as 'Kal'.","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਲ ਮਰਦਾ ਹੈ, ਸ਼ਰੀਰ ਮਰਦਾ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਕਾਲ ਹੀ (ਬਚਨ) ਉਚਾਰਦਾ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੀਭੈ ਗੁਨ ਬਖ੍ਯਾਨ ਹੀ ਸ੍ਰਵਨਨ ਸੁਨਤ ਸੁਧਾਰ। ੫੩।","roman":"Jeebhai gun bakhyaan hee sravnan sunat sudhaar | 53 |","meaning_en":"as the tongue it tells of qualities, and as the ears it listens well.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜੀਭ ਦਾ ਗੁਣ ਬਖਾਨ ਕਰਨਾ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਕੰਨਾ ਦਾ ਕੰਮ ਪੂਰੀ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਸੁਣਨਾ ਹੈ ॥੫੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[54],"number_text":"੫੪।","page":1847,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਲ ਨੈਨ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਸਭਨ ਨਿਹਰਈ। ਕਾਲ ਬਕਤ੍ਰ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਬਾਕ ਉਚਰਈ।","roman":"Kaal nain hvai sabhan nihraee | kaal bakatr hvai baak uchraee |","meaning_en":"Kal, becoming the eyes, looks upon all; Kal, becoming the mouth, utters speech.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਲ ਹੀ ਨੈਣ ਬਣ ਕੇ ਸਭ ਨੂੰ ਵੇਖਦਾ ਹੈ, ਕਾਲ ਮੁਖ ਬਣ ਕੇ ਬਾਣੀ (ਬੋਲ) ਉਚਾਰਦਾ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਲ ਮਰਤ ਕਾਲ ਹੀ ਮਾਰੈ। ਭੂਲਾ ਲੋਗ ਭਰਮ ਬੀਚਾਰੈ। ੫੪।","roman":"Kaal marat kaal hee maarai | bhoolaa log bharam beechaarai | 54 |","meaning_en":"Kal dies and Kal alone kills; deluded people think otherwise in their error.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਲ ਮਰਦਾ ਹੈ ਅਤੇ ਕਾਲ ਹੀ ਮਾਰਦਾ ਹੈ। (ਇਸ ਵਾਸਤਵਿਕਤਾ ਤੋਂ) ਭੁਲੇ ਹੋਏ ਲੋਕੀਂ ਭਰਮਾ ਵਿਚ ਪਏ ਹਨ ॥੫੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[55],"number_text":"੫੫।","page":1847,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਲ ਹਸਤ ਕਾਲੈ ਰੋਵਤ ਕਰਤ ਜਰਾ ਜਿਤ ਹੋਇ।","roman":"Kaal hasat kaalai rovat karat jaraa jit hoi |","meaning_en":"Kal laughs and Kal weeps, and makes old age the victor;","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਰਤ ਜਰਾ ਜਿਤ ਹੋਇ: uncertain, as in verse 51.","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਲ ਹੀ ਹਸਦਾ ਹੈ, ਕਾਲ ਹੀ ਰੋਂਦਾ ਹੈ, ਕਾਲ ਹੀ ਬੁਢਾਪੇ ਉਤੇ ਜਿਤ ਪ੍ਰਾਪਤ ਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਲ ਪਾਇ ਉਪਜਤ ਸਭੈ ਕਾਲ ਪਾਇ ਬਧ ਹੋਇ। ੫੫।","roman":"Kaal paai upjat sabhai kaal paai badh hoi | 55 |","meaning_en":"by Kal all are born, and by Kal they are slain.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਕਾਲ ਪਾਇ: 'on getting their time' or 'through Kal'.","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਲ ਪਾ ਕੇ ਹੀ ਸਭ ਪੈਦਾ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਹਨ ਅਤੇ ਕਾਲ ਪਾ ਕੇ ਹੀ ਮਰਦੇ ਹਨ ॥੫੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[56],"number_text":"੫੬।","page":1847,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਲੈ ਮਰਤ ਕਾਲ ਹੀ ਮਾਰੈ। ਭ੍ਰਮਿ ਭ੍ਰਮਿ ਪਿੰਡ ਅਵਾਰਾ ਪਾਰੈ।","roman":"Kaalai marat kaal hee maarai | bhrami bhrami pind avaaraa paarai |","meaning_en":"Kal dies and Kal alone kills; wandering and wandering, it sets the body adrift.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਪਿੰਡ ਅਵਾਰਾ ਪਾਰੈ: read as 'makes the body a wanderer'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਲ ਹੀ ਮਰਦਾ ਹੈ, ਕਾਲ ਹੀ ਮਾਰਦਾ ਹੈ। (ਕਾਲ ਹੀ) ਆਵਾਗਵਣ ਵਿਚ ਭਰਮ ਭਰਮ ਕੇ ਸ਼ਰੀਰ ('ਪਿੰਡ') ਧਾਰਨ ਕਰਦਾ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕਾਮ ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਮੂਓ ਹੰਕਾਰਾ। ਏਕ ਨ ਮਰਿਯੋ ਸੁ ਬੋਲਣਹਾਰਾ। ੫੬।","roman":"Kaam krodh moo'o hankaaraa | ek na mariyo su bolanhaaraa | 56 |","meaning_en":"Lust, anger and pride have died; one alone has not died, the one who speaks.","page":1847,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਾਮ, ਕ੍ਰੋਧ ਅਤੇ ਹੰਕਾਰ ਮਰਦੇ ਹਨ, (ਪਰ ਕੇਵਲ) ਬੋਲਣ ਵਾਲਾ (ਕਰਤਾਰ) ਨਹੀਂ ਮਰਦਾ ॥੫੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[57],"number_text":"੫੭।","page":1849,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਆਸਾ ਕਰਤ ਸਕਲ ਜਗ ਮਰਈ। ਕੌਨ ਪੁਰਖੁ ਆਸਾ ਪਰਹਰਈ।","roman":"Aasaa karat sakal jag maraee | kaun purkhu aasaa parahraee |","meaning_en":"The whole world dies while still hoping; what man gives up hope?","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਆਸ਼ਾ ਕਰਦਿਆਂ ਕਰਦਿਆਂ ਸਾਰਾ ਜਗਤ ਮਰ ਜਾਦਾ ਹੈ। ਕੌਣ (ਅਜਿਹਾ) ਮਨੁੱਖ ਹੈ ਜੋ ਆਸ਼ਾ ਨੂੰ ਤਿਆਗਦਾ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਨਰ ਕੋਊ ਆਸ ਕੌ ਤ੍ਯਾਗੈ। ਸੋ ਹਰਿ ਕੇ ਪਾਇਨ ਸੌ ਲਾਗੈ। ੫੭।","roman":"Jo nar ko'oo aas kau tyaagai | so hari ke paain sau laagai | 57 |","meaning_en":"Whoever gives up hope is joined to the feet of Hari.","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜੋ ਕੋਈ ਵਿਅਕਤੀ ਆਸ਼ਾ ਨੂੰ ਤਿਆਗ ਦਿੰਦਾ ਹੈ ਉਹ ਪਰਮਾਤਮਾ ਦੇ ਪੈਰਾ ਵਿਚ ਸਥਾਨ ਪਾਦਾ ਹੈ ॥੫੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[58],"number_text":"੫੮।","page":1849,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਆਸਾ ਕੀ ਆਸਾ ਪੁਰਖ ਜੋ ਕੋਊ ਤਜਤ ਬਨਾਇ।","roman":"Aasaa kee aasaa purakh jo ko'oo tajat banaai |","meaning_en":"The man who truly gives up even the hope of hope","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਆਸ਼ਾ ਦੀ ਆਸ ਜੋ ਕੋਈ ਵਿਅਕਤੀ ਤਿਆਗ ਦਿੰਦਾ ਹੈ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਪਾਪ ਪੁੰਨ੍ਯ ਸਰ ਤਰਿ ਤੁਰਤ ਪਰਮ ਪੁਰੀ ਕਹ ਜਾਇ। ੫੮।","roman":"Paap punny sar tari turat param puree kah jaai | 58 |","meaning_en":"at once swims across the lake of sin and merit and goes to the supreme city.'","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਪਾਪ ਪੁੰਨ ਦੇ ਸਰੋਵਰ (ਜਗਤ) ਨੂੰ ਤੁਰਤ ਤਰ ਕੇ ਪਰਮ ਪੁਰੀ ਨੂੰ ਚਲਾ ਜਾਦਾ ਹੈ ॥੫੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[59],"number_text":"੫੯।","page":1849,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜ੍ਯੋ ਸਮੁੰਦਹਿ ਗੰਗਾ ਮਿਲਤ ਸਹੰਸ ਧਾਰ ਕੈ ਸਾਜ।","roman":"Jyo samundhi gangaa milat sahans dhaar kai saaj |","meaning_en":"As the Ganga meets the ocean after forming a thousand streams,","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਵੇਾਂ ਸਮੁੰਦਰ ਵਿਚ ਗੰਗਾ ਹਜ਼ਾਰਾ ਧਾਰਾਵਾ ਬਣਾ ਕੇ ਮਿਲ ਜਾਦੀ ਹੈ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤ੍ਯੋ ਗੋਰਖ ਰਿਖਿਰਾਜ ਸਿਯੋ ਆਜੁ ਮਿਲ੍ਯੋ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਰਾਜ। ੫੯।","roman":"Tyo gorakh rikhiraaj siyo aaju milyo nrip raaj | 59 |","meaning_en":"so today the king of kings met with Gorakh, the king of sages.","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸੇ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਰਿਖੀ ਰਾਜ ਗੋਰਖ ਨਾਲ ਸ਼ਿਰੋਮਣੀ ਰਾਜਾ (ਭਰਥਰੀ) ਮਿਲ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ ॥੫੯॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[60],"number_text":"੬੦।","page":1849,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਯਾਤੇ ਮੈ ਬਿਸਥਾਰ ਨ ਕਰੌ। ਗ੍ਰੰਥ ਬਢਨ ਤੇ ਅਤਿ ਚਿਤ ਡਰੌ।","roman":"Yaate mai bisthaar na karau | granth badhan te ati chit darau |","meaning_en":"For this reason I do not go into detail; I greatly fear in my mind the swelling of the book.","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"The poet speaks.","meaning_pa":"ਇਸ ਲਈ ਮੈਂ ਹੋਰ ਵਿਸਤਾਰ ਵਿਚ ਨਹੀਂ ਪੈਂਦਾ ਕਿਉਾਂਕਿ ਗ੍ਰੰਥ ਦੇ ਵੱਧ ਜਾਣ ਤੋਂ ਮਨ ਵਿਚ ਡਰਦਾ ਹਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਕਥਾ ਨ ਅਧਿਕ ਬਢਾਈ। ਭੂਲ ਪਰੀ ਤਹ ਲੇਹੁ ਬਨਾਈ। ੬੦।","roman":"Taa te kathaa na adhik badhaaee | bhool paree tah lehu banaaee | 60 |","meaning_en":"Therefore I have not made the tale much longer; where there is a mistake, set it right.","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਇਸ ਲਈ ਕਥਾ ਨੂੰ ਅਧਿਕ ਨਹੀਂ ਵਧਾਇਆ। (ਜੇ ਕਿਤੇ) ਭੁਲ ਹੋ ਗਈ ਹੋਵੇ ਤਾ ਸੁਧਾਰ ਲੈਣਾ ॥੬੦॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[61],"number_text":"੬੧।","page":1849,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਗੋਰਖ ਸੋ ਗੋਸਟਿ ਜਬ ਭਈ। ਰਾਜਾ ਕੀ ਦੁਰਮਤਿ ਸਭ ਗਈ।","roman":"Gorakh so gosti jab bhaee | raajaa kee duramti sabh gaee |","meaning_en":"When the discourse with Gorakh had taken place, all the king's wrong thinking went away.","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਦ (ਰਾਜਾ ਭਰਥਰੀ ਹਰਿ ਦੀ) ਗੋਸਟਿ ਗੋਰਖ ਨਾਲ ਹੋਈ ਤਾ ਰਾਜੇ ਦੀ ਦੁਰਬੁੱਧੀ ਖ਼ਤਮ ਹੋ ਗਈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸੀਖਤ ਗ੍ਯਾਨ ਭਲੀ ਬਿਧਿ ਭਯੋ। ਜਲ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਜ੍ਯੋ ਜਲ ਮੈ ਮਿਲਿ ਗਯੋ। ੬੧।","roman":"Seekhat gyaan bhalee bidhi bhayo | jal hvai jyo jal mai mili gayo | 61 |","meaning_en":"He learned wisdom in a good way, and merged like water into water.","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਉਸ ਨੇ) ਚੰਗੀ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਨਾਲ ਗਿਆਨ ਸਿਖ ਲਿਆ ਅਤੇ (ਗੋਰਖ ਨਾਲ ਇੰਜ ਮਿਲ ਗਿਆ) ਜਿਵੇਾਂ ਜਲ ਨਾਲ ਜਲ ਮਿਲ ਜਾਦਾ ਹੈ ॥੬੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਅੜਿਲ","gurmukhi":"ਅੜਿਲ","roman":"Aril","meaning_en":"Arril.","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੜਿਲ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[62],"number_text":"੬੨।","page":1849,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਏਕ ਮੂੰਡ ਭਰਥਰਿ ਘ੍ਰਿਤ ਚੁਅਤ ਨਿਹਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Ek moond bharathri ghrit chuat nihaariyo |","meaning_en":"Bharthari saw a head dripping with ghee;","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮੂੰਡ: 'head'; perhaps a skull or a pot-shaped vessel; the story behind the verse is not given; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"(ਕਿਸੇ ਦਿਨ ਭਿਖਿਆ ਮੰਗਦਿਆਂ) ਭਰਥਰੀ ਨੇ (ਇਕ ਚਰਖੇ ਦਾ) ਮੁੰਨਾ ਵੇਖਿਆ (ਜਿਸ ਵਿਚੋਂ ਗਰਮੀ ਕਰ ਕੇ) ਘਿਓ ਚੋ ਰਿਹਾ ਸੀ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹਸਿ ਹਸਿ ਤਾ ਸੋ ਬਚਨ ਇਹ ਭਾਤਿ ਉਚਾਰਿਯੋ।","roman":"Hasi hasi taa so bachan ih bhaati uchaariyo |","meaning_en":"laughing and laughing, he spoke to it in this way:","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਉਸ ਚਰਖਾ ਕੱਤਣ ਵਾਲੀ ਪ੍ਰਤਿ ਭਰਥਰੀ ਨੇ) ਹਸ ਕੇ ਇਸ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਬੋਲ ਉਚਾਰਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਿਨ ਕੋ ਲਗੇ ਕਟਾਛ ਰਾਜ ਤੇ ਖੋਵਹੀ।","roman":"Jin ko lage kataachh raaj te khovhee |","meaning_en":"'Those who are struck by a woman's sidelong glance lose their kingdoms;","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"'a woman's' is understood from ਕਟਾਛ, the sidelong glance.","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਨ੍ਰਹਾ ਨੂੰ (ਇਸਤਰੀ ਦੀ) ਕਟਾਖ ਲਗ ਜਾਵੇ, ਉਹ ਰਾਜ ਖੋਹ ਦਿੰਦੇ ਹਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਤੁਹਿ ਕਰ ਲਾਗੇ ਤੈ ਕ੍ਯੋ ਮੂਢ ਨ ਰੋਵਹੀ। ੬੨।","roman":"Ho tuhi kar laage tai kyo moodh na rovhee | 62 |","meaning_en":"you have been touched by her hand; why then, fool, do you not weep?'","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਤੁਹਿ ਕਰ ਲਾਗੇ: 'the hand has touched you'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਹੇ ਚਰਖੇ ਦੇ ਮੁੰਨੇ! ਤੈਨੂੰ ਤਾ (ਇਸਤਰੀ ਦੇ) ਹੱਥ ਲਗ ਗਏ ਹਨ, ਭਲਾ ਤੂੰ ਕਿਉਾਂ ਨਾ ਰੋਵੇਾਂ ॥੬੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[63],"number_text":"੬੩।","page":1849,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਬੀਤਤ ਬਰਖ ਬਹੁਤ ਜਬ ਭਏ। ਭਰਥਰਿ ਦੇਸ ਆਪਨੇ ਗਏ।","roman":"Beetat barakh bahut jab bhae | bharathri des aapne gae |","meaning_en":"When many years had gone by, Bharthari went to his own country.","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਦ ਬਹੁਤ ਸਾਲ ਬੀਤ ਗਏ ਤਾ ਭਰਥਰੀ ਆਪਣੇ ਦੇਸ ਗਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਚੀਨਤ ਏਕ ਚੰਚਲਾ ਭਈ। ਨਿਕਟ ਰਾਨਿਯਨ ਕੇ ਚਲਿ ਗਈ। ੬੩।","roman":"Cheenat ek chanchlaa bhaee | nikat raaniyan ke chali gaee | 63 |","meaning_en":"A woman recognised him, and went to the queens.","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਉਥੋਂ ਦੀ) ਇਕ ਇਸਤਰੀ ਨੇ (ਰਾਜੇ ਨੂੰ) ਪਛਾਣ ਲਿਆ ਅਤੇ ਰਾਣੀਆਂ ਦੇ ਕੋਲ ਚਲੀ ਗਈ ॥੬੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[64],"number_text":"੬੪।","page":1849,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨਿ ਰਾਨਿਯਨ ਐਸੋ ਬਚਨ ਰਾਜਾ ਲਿਯੋ ਬੁਲਾਇ।","roman":"Suni raaniyan aiso bachan raajaa liyo bulaai |","meaning_en":"Hearing such news, the queens had the king called;","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਜਿਹੀ ਗੱਲ ਸੁਣ ਕੇ ਰਾਣੀਆਂ ਨੇ ਰਾਜੇ ਨੂੰ (ਆਪਣੇ ਕੋਲ) ਬੁਲਾ ਲਿਆ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਭਾਤਿ ਭਾਤਿ ਰੋਦਨ ਕਰਤ ਰਹੀ ਚਰਨ ਲਪਟਾਇ। ੬੪।","roman":"Bhaati bhaati rodan karat rahee charan laptaai | 64 |","meaning_en":"weeping in many ways, they clung to his feet.","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਈ ਤਰ੍ਰਹਾ ਦਾ ਰੋਣਾ ਧੋਣਾ ਕਰ ਕੇ (ਰਾਜੇ ਦੇ) ਚਰਨਾ ਨਾਲ ਲਿਪਟ ਗਈਆਂ ॥੬੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","gurmukhi":"ਸੋਰਠਾ","roman":"Sorthaa","meaning_en":"Sortha.","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਸੋਰਠਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[65],"number_text":"੬੫।","page":1849,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਸਾ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਨ ਮਾਸ ਰਕਤ ਰੰਚ ਤਨ ਨ ਰਹਿਯੋ।","roman":"Maasaa rahiyo na maas rakat ranch tan na rahiyo |","meaning_en":"'Not a masha of flesh is left, not a trace of blood is left in the body;","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਮਾਸਾ: a masha, a very small weight.","meaning_pa":"(ਰਾਣੀਆਂ ਕਹਿਣ ਲਗੀਆਂ) ਸ਼ਰੀਰ ਵਿਚ ਮਾਸਾ ਜਿੰਨਾ ਵੀ ਮਾਸ ਨਹੀਂ ਰਿਹਾ ਅਤੇ ਨਾ ਹੀ ਰਤਾ ਜਿੰਨਾ ਲਹੂ ਰਿਹਾ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸ੍ਵਾਸ ਨ ਉਡ੍ਯੋ ਉਸਾਸ ਆਸ ਤਿਹਾਰੈ ਮਿਲਨ ਕੀ। ੬੫।","roman":"Svaas na udyo usaas aas tihaarai milan kee | 65 |","meaning_en":"the breath has not flown off with our sighs, only in the hope of meeting you.","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਭੇ ਸੁਆਸਾ ਨਾਲ ਸੁਆਸ ਨਹੀਂ ਉਡੇ (ਕਿਉਾਂਕਿ) ਤੁਹਾਡੇ ਮਿਲਣ ਦੀ ਆਸ ਸੀ ॥੬੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[66],"number_text":"੬੬।","page":1849,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋਗ ਕੀਯੋ ਪੂਰਨ ਭਯੋ ਨ੍ਰਿਪ ਬਰ। ਅਬ ਤੁਮ ਰਾਜ ਕਰੋ ਸੁਖ ਸੌ ਘਰ।","roman":"Jog keeyo pooran bhayo nrip bar | ab tum raaj karo sukh sau ghar |","meaning_en":"You have practised yoga and become perfect, excellent king; now rule at home in comfort.","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹੇ ਸ੍ਰੇਸ਼ਠ ਰਾਜੇ! ਤੁਸੀਂ ਯੋਗ ਸਾਧਨਾ ਕਰ ਕੇ ਪੂਰਨ ਹੋ ਗਏ ਹੋ। ਹੁਣ ਤੁਸੀਂ ਸੁਖ ਪੂਰਵਕ ਘਰ ਵਿਚ ਰਾਜ ਕਰੋ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੌ ਸਭਹਿਨ ਹਮ ਪ੍ਰਥਮ ਸੰਘਾਰੋ। ਤਾ ਪਾਛੇ ਬਨ ਓਰ ਸਿਧਾਰੋ। ੬੬।","roman":"Jau sabhhin ham pratham sanghaaro | taa paachhe ban or sidhaaro | 66 |","meaning_en":"Or else first kill all of us, and after that set out for the forest.'","page":1849,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜੌ: 'if'; read as 'or else'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਜਾ (ਤੁਸੀਂ ਹੁਣ) ਅਸਾ ਸਾਰੀਆਂ ਨੂੰ ਪਹਿਲਾ ਮਾਰ ਦਿਓ ਤਾ ਪਿਛੋਂ ਬਨ ਵਲ ਜਾਓ ॥੬੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"speaker","name":"ਭਰਥਰਿ ਬਾਚ","gurmukhi":"ਭਰਥਰਿ ਬਾਚ","roman":"Bharathri baach","meaning_en":"Bharthari said:","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਭਰਥਰੀ ਨੇ ਕਿਹਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[67],"number_text":"੬੭।","page":1851,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੇ ਰਾਨੀ ਜੋਬਨ ਭਰੀ ਅਧਿਕ ਤਬੈ ਗਰਬਾਹਿ।","roman":"Je raanee joban bharee adhik tabai garbaahi |","meaning_en":"'The queens who then were full of youth and very proud","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਹੜੀਆਂ ਰਾਣੀਆਂ ਉਦੋਂ ਜੋਬਨਵੰਤ ਸਨ, ਅਤੇ ਬਹੁਤ ਹੰਕਾਰ ਕਰਦੀਆਂ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੇ ਅਬ ਰੂਪ ਰਹਿਤ ਭਈ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਗਰਬ ਕਛੁ ਨਾਹਿ। ੬੭।","roman":"Te ab roop rahit bhaee rahiyo garab kachhu naahi | 67 |","meaning_en":"have now become bereft of beauty; no pride at all remains.","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਹ ਹੁਣ ਰੂਪ ਤੋਂ ਰਹਿਤ ਹੋ ਗਈਆਂ ਹਨ, ਉਨ੍ਰਹਾ ਵਿਚ ਕੁਝ ਵੀ ਹੰਕਾਰ ਨਹੀਂ ਰਿਹਾ ॥੬੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[68],"number_text":"੬੮।","page":1851,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਅਬਲਾ ਹੁਤੀ ਤਰੁਨਿ ਤੇ ਭਈ। ਤਰੁਨਿ ਜੁ ਹੁਤੀ ਬ੍ਰਿਧ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਗਈ।","roman":"Ablaa hutee taruni te bhaee | taruni ju hutee bridh hvai gaee |","meaning_en":"She who was a girl became a young woman; she who was a young woman became old.","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਬਲਾ: 'woman'; read here as 'girl' (ਬਾਲਾ) for the contrast; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਜੋ (ਉਦੋਂ) ਅਬਲਾ ਸੀ, ਉਹ ਜਵਾਨ ਹੋ ਗਈ ਅਤੇ ਜੋ ਜੁਆਨ ਸੀ ਉਹ ਬੁੱਢੀ ਹੋ ਗਈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਿਰਧਨਿ ਤੇ ਕੋਊ ਲਹੀ ਨ ਜਾਵੈ। ਚਿਤ ਕੌ ਇਹੈ ਅਸਚਰਜ ਆਵੈ। ੬੮।","roman":"Biradhni te ko'oo lahee na jaavai | chit kau ihai asachraj aavai | 68 |","meaning_en":"Of those who were old, not one is to be found; this is the wonder that comes to my mind.","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜੋ ਬਿਰਧ ਸਨ (ਉਨ੍ਰਹਾ ਵਿਚੋਂ) ਕੋਈ ਦਿਸਦੀ ਨਹੀਂ ਹੈ। ਚਿਤ ਵਿਚ ਇਹੀ ਹੈਰਾਨੀ ਹੁੰਦੀ ਹੈ ॥੬੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[69],"number_text":"੬੯।","page":1851,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੇ ਰਾਨੀ ਜੋਬਨ ਕੀ ਭਰੀ। ਤੇ ਅਬ ਭਈ ਜਰਾ ਕੀ ਧਰੀ।","roman":"Je raanee joban kee bharee | te ab bhaee jaraa kee dharee |","meaning_en":"The queens who were full of youth have now been seized by old age.","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਹੜੀਆਂ ਰਾਣੀਆਂ (ਉਦੋਂ) ਜੋਬਨ ਨਾਲ ਭਰੀਆਂ ਹੋਈਆਂ ਸਨ, ਉਨ੍ਰਹਾ ਨੂੰ ਬੁਢਾਪੇ ਨੇ ਕਾਬੂ ਕਰ ਲਿਆ ਹੈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੇ ਅਬਲਾ ਸੁੰਦਰ ਗਰਬਾਹੀ। ਤਿਨ ਕੋ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਗਰਬ ਕਛੁ ਨਾਹੀ। ੬੯।","roman":"Je ablaa sundar garbaahee | tin ko rahiyo garab kachhu naahee | 69 |","meaning_en":"The beautiful women who were proud have no pride at all left.","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਿਹੜੀਆਂ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਸੁੰਦਰਤਾ ਕਰ ਕੇ ਹੰਕਾਰੀਆਂ ਹੋਈਆਂ ਸਨ, ਉਨ੍ਰਹਾ ਦਾ ਗਰਬ ਬਿਲਕੁਲ ਖ਼ਤਮ ਹੋ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ ॥੬੯॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[70],"number_text":"੭੦।","page":1851,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੇ ਮਨ ਮੈ ਗਰਬਤ ਤਬੈ ਅਧਿਕ ਚੰਚਲਾ ਨਾਰਿ।","roman":"Je man mai garbat tabai adhik chanchlaa naari |","meaning_en":"The restless women who then were very proud in their minds","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜੋ ਅਧਿਕ ਚੰਚਲ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਉਦੋਂ ਮਨ ਵਿਚ ਬਹੁਤ ਅਭਿਮਾਨ ਕਰਦੀਆਂ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤੇ ਅਬ ਜੀਤਿ ਜਰਾ ਲਈ ਸਕਤ ਨ ਦੇਹ ਸੰਭਾਰਿ। ੭੦।","roman":"Te ab jeeti jaraa laee sakat na deh sanbhaari | 70 |","meaning_en":"have now been conquered by old age; they cannot hold up their bodies.","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਨ੍ਰਹਾ ਨੂੰ ਹੁਣ ਬੁਢਾਪੇ ਨੇ ਜਿਤ ਲਿਆ ਹੈ, (ਉਹ) ਸ਼ਰੀਰ ਨੂੰ ਵੀ ਸੰਭਾਲ ਨਹੀਂ ਸਕਦੀਆਂ ॥੭੦॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[71],"number_text":"੭੧।","page":1851,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੇ ਜੇ ਤ੍ਰਿਯਾ ਤਬੈ ਗਰਬਾਹੀ। ਤਿਨ ਕੇ ਰਹਿਯੋ ਗਰਬ ਕਛੁ ਨਾਹੀ।","roman":"Je je triyaa tabai garbaahee | tin ke rahiyo garab kachhu naahee |","meaning_en":"Each and every woman who then was proud has no pride at all left.","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜੋ ਜੋ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਉਦੋਂ ਮਾਣ ਕਰਦੀਆਂ ਸਨ, ਉਨ੍ਰਹਾ ਦਾ ਹੁਣ ਕੁਝ ਵੀ ਮਾਣ ਨਹੀਂ ਰਿਹਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਰੁਨੀ ਹੁਤੀ ਬਿਰਧ ਤੇ ਭਈ। ਠੌਰੈ ਠੌਰ ਔਰ ਹ੍ਵੈ ਗਈ। ੭੧।","roman":"Tarunee hutee biradh te bhaee | thaurai thaur aur hvai gaee | 71 |","meaning_en":"Those who were young became old; in every part they have become other than they were.","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜੋ ਜਵਾਨ ਸਨ, ਉਹ ਬਿਰਧ ਹੋ ਗਈਆਂ ਹਨ। ਹੌਲੀ ਹੌਲੀ ਹੋਰ ਦੀਆਂ ਹੋਰ ਹੋ ਗਈਆਂ ਹਨ ॥੭੧॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[72],"number_text":"੭੨।","page":1851,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੇਸਨ ਪ੍ਰਭਾ ਜਾਤ ਨਹਿ ਕਹੀ। ਜਾਨੁਕ ਜਟਨ ਜਾਨਵੀ ਬਹੀ।","roman":"Kesan prabhaa jaat nahi kahee | jaanuk jatan jaanvee bahee |","meaning_en":"The radiance of your hair cannot be told; it is as if the Ganga flowed through matted locks,","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਜਾਨਵੀ: Jahnavi, the Ganga, flowing white through Shiva's locks.","meaning_pa":"(ਉਨ੍ਰਹਾ ਦੇ) ਕੇਸਾ ਦੀ ਸ਼ੋਭਾ ਦਾ ਵਰਣਨ ਨਹੀਂ ਕੀਤਾ ਜਾ ਸਕਦਾ ਸੀ, (ਪਰ ਹੁਣ ਉਹ ਇੰਜ ਪ੍ਰਤੀਤ ਹੋ ਰਹੇ ਹਨ) ਮਾਨੋ (ਸ਼ਿਵ ਦੀਆਂ) ਜਟਾਵਾ ਵਿਚ ਗੰਗਾ ਵਗ ਰਹੀ ਹੋਵੇ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਕੈਧੋ ਸਕਲ ਦੁਗਧ ਸੌ ਧੋਏ। ਤਾ ਤੇ ਸੇਤ ਬਰਨ ਕਚ ਹੋਏ। ੭੨।","roman":"Kaidho sakal dugadh sau dhoe | taa te set baran kach hoe | 72 |","meaning_en":"or as if all of it had been washed in milk, and so the hair has turned white in colour.","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਾ ਸਾਰੇ ਕੇਸ ਦੁੱਧ ਨਾਲ ਧੋਏ ਗਏ ਹੋਣ, ਇਸ ਕਰ ਕੇ ਸਫ਼ੈਦ ਰੰਗ ਵਾਲੇ ਹੋ ਗਏ ਹਨ ॥੭੨॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[73],"number_text":"੭੩।","page":1851,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮੁਕਤਨ ਹੀਰਨ ਕੇ ਬਹੁਤ ਇਨ ਪਰ ਕੀਏ ਸਿੰਗਾਰ।","roman":"Muktan heeran ke bahut in par kee'e singaar |","meaning_en":"Many adornments of pearls and diamonds were put on these;","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"(ਕਦੇ) ਇਨ੍ਰਹਾ ਉਤੇ ਹੀਰਿਆਂ ਅਤੇ ਮੋਤੀਆਂ ਦੇ ਸ਼ਿੰਗਾਰ ਕੀਤੇ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਾ ਤੇ ਤਿਨ ਕੀ ਛਬਿ ਭਏ ਤਰੁਨਿ ਤਿਹਾਰੇ ਬਾਰ। ੭੩।","roman":"Taa te tin kee chhabi bhae taruni tihaare baar | 73 |","meaning_en":"therefore, young woman, your hair has taken on their lustre.","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਇਸ ਲਈ ਹੇ ਇਸਤਰੀਓ! ਤੁਹਾਡੇ ਇਨ੍ਰਹਾ ਵਾਲਾ ਦੀ ਛਬੀ ਉਨ੍ਰਹਾ ਵਰਗੀ (ਸਫ਼ੈਦ) ਹੋ ਗਈ ਹੈ ॥੭੩॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[74],"number_text":"੭੪।","page":1851,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਤਬ ਅਤਿ ਸੋਭਿਤ ਹੁਤੇ ਤਰੁਨਿ ਤਿਹਾਰੇ ਕੇਸ।","roman":"Jo tab ati sobhit hute taruni tihaare kes |","meaning_en":"Your hair, young woman, which then was so very beautiful,","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਹੇ ਇਸਤਰੀਓ! ਤਦ ਜੋ ਤੁਹਾਡੇ ਕੇਸ ਬਹੁਤ ਸ਼ੋਭਦੇ ਸਨ,","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਨੀਲ ਮਨੀ ਕੀ ਛਬਿ ਹੁਤੇ ਭਏ ਰੁਕਮ ਕੇ ਭੇਸ। ੭੪।","roman":"Neel manee kee chhabi hute bhae rukam ke bhes | 74 |","meaning_en":"which had the lustre of sapphire, has taken on the look of silver.","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਰੁਕਮ: gold or silver; silver here.","meaning_pa":"ਨੀਲਮਣੀ ਦੇ ਛਬੀ ਵਾਲੇ ਹੁੰਦੇ ਸਨ (ਹੁਣ) ਚਾਦੀ ਦੇ ਰੰਗ ਵਾਲੇ ਹੋ ਗਏ ਹਨ ॥੭੪॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਚੌਪਈ","gurmukhi":"ਚੌਪਈ","roman":"Chaupaee","meaning_en":"Chaupai.","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਚੌਪਈ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[75],"number_text":"੭੫।","page":1851,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਕੈਧੋ ਸਕਲ ਪੁਹਪ ਗੁਹਿ ਡਾਰੇ। ਤਾ ਤੇ ਕਚ ਸਿਤ ਭਏ ਤਿਹਾਰੇ।","roman":"Kaidho sakal puhap guhi daare | taa te kach sit bhae tihaare |","meaning_en":"Or perhaps all the flowers were strung into it, and so your hair became white;","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਾ ਸਾਰਿਆਂ ਨਾਲ ਫੁਲ ਗੁੰਦ ਦਿੱਤੇ ਹੋਣ, ਇਸ ਲਈ ਤੁਹਾਡੇ ਵਾਲ ਸਫ਼ੈਦ ਹੋ ਗਏ ਹਨ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਸਿ ਕੀ ਜੌਨਿ ਅਧਿਕਧੌ ਪਰੀ। ਤਾ ਤੇ ਸਕਲ ਸ੍ਯਾਮਤਾ ਹਰੀ। ੭੫।","roman":"Sasi kee jauni adhikdhau paree | taa te sakal syaamtaa haree | 75 |","meaning_en":"or the light of the moon fell on it too strongly, and so took all its blackness away.'","page":1851,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਅਧਿਕਧੌ: 'much, or perhaps'.","meaning_pa":"ਜਾ ਚੰਦ੍ਰਮਾ ਦੀ ਚਾਦਨੀ ('ਜੌਨਿ') ਅਧਿਕ ਪੈ ਗਈ ਹੈ, ਜਿਸ ਕਰ ਕੇ ਸਾਰਾ ਕਾਲਾਪਨ ਖ਼ਤਮ ਹੋ ਗਿਆ ਹੈ ॥੭੫॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਅੜਿਲ","gurmukhi":"ਅੜਿਲ","roman":"Aril","meaning_en":"Arril.","page":1853,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅੜਿਲ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[76],"number_text":"੭੬।","page":1853,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਕ ਰਾਨੀ ਤਬ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਨ੍ਰਿਪਹਿ ਸਮਝਾਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Ik raanee tab kahiyo nriphi samjhaai kai |","meaning_en":"Then one queen spoke, reasoning with the king:","page":1853,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਤਦ ਇਕ ਰਾਣੀ ਨੇ ਰਾਜੇ ਨੂੰ ਸਮਝਾ ਕੇ ਕਿਹਾ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਮੁਹਿ ਗੋਰਖ ਕਹਿ ਗਏ ਸੁਪਨ ਮੈ ਆਇ ਕੈ।","roman":"Muhi gorakh kahi gae supan mai aai kai |","meaning_en":"'Gorakh came to me in a dream and told me:","page":1853,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿ ਮੈਨੂੰ ਸੁਪਨੇ ਵਿਚ ਆ ਕੇ ਗੋਰਖ ਨਾਥ ਕਹਿ ਗਏ ਸਨ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜਬ ਲੌ ਤ੍ਰਿਯ ਏ ਜਿਯਤ ਰਾਜ ਤਬ ਲੌ ਕਰੌ।","roman":"Jab lau triy e jiyat raaj tab lau karau |","meaning_en":"\"As long as these women live, so long rule the kingdom;","page":1853,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਕਿ ਜਦ ਤਕ ਇਹ ਇਸਤਰੀਆਂ ਜੀਉਾਂਦੀਆਂ ਹਨ, ਤਦ ਤਕ (ਤੁਸੀਂ) ਰਾਜ ਕਰੋ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਜਬ ਏ ਸਭ ਮਰਿ ਜੈ ਹੈ ਤਬ ਪਗ ਮਗ ਧਰੋ। ੭੬।","roman":"Ho jab e sabh mari jai hai tab pag mag dharo | 76 |","meaning_en":"when they have all died, then set your foot upon the road.\"'","page":1853,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜਦ ਇਹ ਸਾਰੀਆਂ ਮਰ ਜਾਣਗੀਆਂ ਤਦ ਤੁਸੀਂ (ਯੋਗ ਦੇ) ਮਾਰਗ ਉਤੇ ਕਦਮ ਰਖਣਾ ॥੭੬॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"verse","number":[77],"number_text":"੭੭।","page":1853,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਸੁਨਿ ਰਨਿਯਨ ਕੇ ਬਚਨ ਨ੍ਰਿਪਹਿ ਕਰੁਣਾ ਭਈ।","roman":"Suni raniyan ke bachan nriphi karunaa bhaee |","meaning_en":"Hearing the words of the queens, the king felt compassion;","page":1853,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਣੀਆਂ ਦੇ ਬਚਨ ਸੁਣ ਕੇ ਰਾਜੇ (ਦੇ ਮਨ ਵਿਚ) ਕਰੁਣਾ ਪੈਦਾ ਹੋ ਗਈ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਤਿਨ ਕੈ ਭੀਤਰ ਬੁਧ ਕਛੁਕ ਅਪੁਨੀ ਦਈ।","roman":"Tin kai bheetar budh kachhuk apunee daee |","meaning_en":"he put something of his own understanding into them.","page":1853,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਉਸ ਨੇ ਉਨ੍ਰਹਾ ਵਿਚ ਕੁਝ ਆਪਣਾ ਗਿਆਨ ਦਾਖਲ ਕੀਤਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਜੋ ਕਛੁ ਪਿੰਗੁਲ ਕਹਿਯੋ ਮਾਨ ਸੋਈ ਲਿਯੋ।","roman":"Jo kachhu pingul kahiyo maan soee liyo |","meaning_en":"Whatever Pingula said, that he accepted;","page":1853,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਜੋ ਕੁਝ ਪਿੰਗੁਲਾ (ਰਾਣੀ) ਨੇ ਕਿਹਾ, ਉਹੀ ਮੰਨ ਲਿਆ","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਹੋ ਰਾਜ ਜੋਗ ਘਰ ਬੈਠ ਦੋਊ ਅਪਨੇ ਕਿਯੋ। ੭੭।","roman":"Ho raaj jog ghar baith do'oo apne kiyo | 77 |","meaning_en":"sitting at home, he made both kingship and yoga his own.","page":1853,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਅਤੇ ਘਰ ਵਿਚ ਬੈਠ ਕੇ ਰਾਜ ਅਤੇ ਯੋਗ ਦੋਵੇਾਂ ਕੀਤੇ ॥੭੭॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]},{"type":"heading","kind":"chhand","name":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","gurmukhi":"ਦੋਹਰਾ","roman":"Dohraa","meaning_en":"Dohra.","page":1853,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਦੋਹਰਾ:","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"type":"verse","number":[78,1],"number_text":"੭੮। ੧।","page":1853,"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਮਾਨਿ ਰਾਨਿਯਨ ਕੋ ਬਚਨ ਰਾਜ ਕਰਿਯੋ ਸੁਖ ਮਾਨਿ।","roman":"Maani raaniyan ko bachan raaj kariyo sukh maani |","meaning_en":"Heeding the word of the queens, he ruled the kingdom in comfort;","page":1853,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਰਾਣੀਆਂ ਦੇ ਬਚਨ ਮੰਨ ਕੇ (ਭਰਥਰੀ ਨੇ) ਸੁਖ ਪੂਰਵਕ ਰਾਜ ਕੀਤਾ।","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"},{"gurmukhi":"ਬਹੁਰਿ ਪਿੰਗੁਲ ਕੇ ਮਰੇ ਬਨ ਕੌ ਕਿਯੋ ਪਯਾਨ। ੭੮। ੧।","roman":"Bahuri pingul ke mare ban kau kiyo payaan | 78 | 1 |","meaning_en":"then, when Pingula died, he set out for the forest.","page":1853,"meaning_status":"draft","meaning_pa":"ਫਿਰ ਪਿੰਗੁਲਾ ਦੇ ਮਰਨ ਤੇ ਬਨ ਨੂੰ ਚਲਾ ਗਿਆ ॥੭੮॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB"}]}],"ending":{"lines":[{"gurmukhi":"ਇਤਿ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਚਰਿਤ੍ਰ ਪਖ੍ਯਾਨੇ ਤ੍ਰਿਯਾ ਚਰਿਤ੍ਰੇ ਮੰਤ੍ਰੀ ਭੂਪ ਸੰਬਾਦੇ ਦੋਇ ਸੌ ਨੌ ਚਰਿਤ੍ਰ ਸਮਾਪਤਮ","roman":"Iti sree charitr pakhyaane triyaa charitre mantree bhoop sanbaade doi sau nau charitr samaaptam","meaning_en":"Thus ends the two hundred and ninth charitra of the Charitropakhyan, of the wiles of women, in the dialogue of the minister and the king; complete.","page":1853,"meaning_status":"draft"},{"gurmukhi":"ਸਤੁ ਸੁਭਮ ਸਤੁ। ੨੦੯। ੪੦੧੨। ਅਫਜੂੰ।","roman":"Satu subham satu | 209 | 4012 | aphjoon |","meaning_en":"True, auspicious, true. 209. 4012. It continues.","page":1853,"meaning_status":"draft","note":"ਸਤੁ ਸੁਭਮ ਸਤੁ: a closing benediction; read as 'may it be auspicious' (ਸਤੁ as 'may it be'); ਸਤੁ could also be 'true'; uncertain. The numbers are the charitra number and the running verse count. ਅਫਜੂੰ: Persian afzun, 'more', taken as 'more follows'; uncertain.","meaning_pa":"ਇਥੇ ਸ੍ਰੀ ਚਰਿਤ੍ਰੋਪਾਖਿਆਨ ਦੇ ਤ੍ਰੀਆ ਚਰਿਤ੍ਰ ਦੇ ਮੰਤ੍ਰੀ ਭੂਪ ਸੰਵਾਦ ਦੇ ੨੦੯ਵੇਾਂ ਚਰਿਤ੍ਰ ਦੀ ਸਮਾਪਤੀ, ਸਭ ਸ਼ੁਭ ਹੈ ॥੨੦੯॥੪੦੧੨॥ ਚਲਦਾ॥","meaning_pa_source":"BaniDB","note_pa":"ਇਹ ਅਰਥ ਇਸ ਪੰਕਤੀ ਸਮੇਤ ਉੱਪਰਲੀਆਂ 2 ਪੰਕਤੀਆਂ ਦਾ ਇਕੱਠਾ ਹੈ।"}],"page":1853,"number":[209,4012]}});
